    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/clinical-laboratory-manager-internal-posting-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** - Main Campus",
      "description": "Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** 511369 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 560115 - SHC - Laboratory Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites *** This Posting is open to current employees of Mississippi State University**** Position Function: Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Salary Grade : 15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The following examples are intended as illustrations only of the various duties assigned to this position. The absence of specific statements of duties does not exclude those tasks from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment of the position. 1. Performs Supervisory /Administrative Duties a. Coaches, counsels, and disciplines employees as necessary b. Ensures new Medical Technologist and Assistants are trained properly c. Interviews candidates and gives recommendation to hire or not hire to directors d. Approves time off e. Writes and conducts performance reviews of lab employees f. Maintains inventory and orders supplies g. Maintains computer records h. Maintains statistical reports i. Implements new procedures 2. Performs Medical Technologist Duties a. Trains new Medical Technologist: and Lab Assistants( to perform basic lab tests) b. Performs controls on instruments daily, and kits at time of lot number change or shipment date change. c. Calibrates the lab equipment d. Ensues hazardous waste is disposed of properly e. Performs standard laboratory tests. f. Keep accurate daily records g. Collect and prepare specimens for testing and sending to reference lab h. Follow quality control procedures 3. Performs Miscellaneous Duties a. Provides pleasant, prompt service to patients b. Performs other responsibilities as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor of Science Degree in Medical Technology Registered as Medical Technologist with the American Society of Clinical Pathologist Two years experience as a Medical Technologist Excellent verbal communication skills ABDs or degree pending considered (all but DISS): Preferred Qualifications: Experience beyond the minimum requirement of two years as a Medical Technologist. Previous experience as a Clinical Laboratory Manager. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Responsible for carrying out broad assignments and tasks under very limited direction. Knowledge, skills and abilities commensurate with having met the minimum job requirements. Working Conditions and Physical Effort General office conditions. Exposure to potentially infectious body fluids Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Please apply online at https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/search Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 02683e2b Last Name (required) cfc49978 Email (required) f18a49d6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Facilities Supervisor Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The management and operation of the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station (MAFES) Horse Unit located at the H.H. Levick Animal Research Center. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert dccb4b44 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 940ae4a7 Last Name (required) e2331654 Email (required) e8d13e8e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
