    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/campus-security-officer-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-f4eeed8e-7cd7-43f7-8f3e-dcc017c3b814": {
      "title": "Campus Security Officer - Main Campus",
      "description": "Campus Security Officer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Campus Security Officer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Campus Security Officer 511377 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 470900 - Police Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 14 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: This position is a non-sworn, uniformed officer. The following examples are intended as illustrations only of the various types of duties assigned in positions allocated to this classification. The absence of specific statements of duties does not exclude those tasks from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment of the position. Salary Grade : 10 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Mississippi State University Police Department is charged with providing for the safety of all the students, faculty, staff, and guests who attend class, work, live, and visit our campus, and with the security of university buildings and property. Mississippi State University police officers are always working and available to assist you. The department provides a comprehensive array of law enforcement services through a dedicated staff of more than 35 sworn, state commissioned police officers and 16 full-time support personnel. All MSU Police officers are certified by the Mississippi Peace Officers Minimum Standards Commission and have the same authorities and must meet the same expectations as law enforcement officers in any community. Area of Specialization: Campus Security Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Performs foot and vehicle patrols of campus areas to monitor behavior, buildings, and property and communicates necessary campus safety information to the University Police Department. 2. Physically secure buildings as scheduled. 3. Opening and securing rooms and buildings at the request of authorized individuals. 4. Providing safety escorts as needed. 5. Patrols campus buildings and property to ensure the security of the facilities/areas. 6. Escort maintenance personnel to assigned areas for repairs after hours. 7. Maintain radio communications with other safety personnel and officers on campus. 8. Responds to activation of alarm systems including campus-wide electronic sensor alarm alerts. 9. Write and submit incident reports to assigned supervisor or law enforcement officer. 10. Other duties may include training additional security officers and assisting with crowd control and/or directing traffic during special events. 11. Ability to work in stressful situations and deescalate potential violent activity. 12. Perform other assigned work-related duties as required. The above essential duties are representative of major duties in this position. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Other duties may be assigned to the above consistent with the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for the job. Not all of the duties may be assigned to a position. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High School diploma or equivalent. Experience: Two (2) years of previous work experience. Focus: Security related acumen. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Education beyond the minimum. 2. Previous work experience. 3. Certification in CPR/ First Aid. 4. Good physical condition. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Ability to work within a team and foster professionalism in job assignments. 2. Ability to work in stressful situations and deescalate potential violent activity. 3. Demonstrate vigilance for safety and deterrence of criminal activity. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Must be available to work rotating shifts (including nights and weekends), outdoors, and in a variety of assignments including foot, vehicle, and bicycle patrol. 2. Regularly involves lifting, bending or other physical exertion. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. 3. Frequent-Externally imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one's control. 4. Job requires sitting, standing, stooping, kneeling, crouching, lifting, walking, reaching, climbing, talking, hearing and handling objects. 5. Ability to see information in print and/or electronically, ability to distinguish colors. Instructions for Applying: Please apply online. Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 223bc3dd Last Name (required) 8c47dbbc Email (required) 496e9c53 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 9d84d2eb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 2fcf1bc0 Last Name (required) e61a7348 Email (required) 4e8979d3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
