    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/icu-technician-trainee-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-1056cc68-9771-494c-b504-f64b150756ca": {
      "title": "ICU Technician Trainee - Main Campus",
      "description": "ICU Technician Trainee - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States ICU Technician Trainee - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! ICU Technician Trainee 511378 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 184100 - CVM AHC Administration Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 13 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The ICU technician position provides primary care to all emergency patients and advanced care for critical patients of the Animal Health Center (AHC) along with support for hospitalized patients. Though legally limited to providing patient care except for diagnosing, prescribing, or performing surgery; these vital technicians are responsible for executing the wishes of the veterinary medical doctor team and monitoring patient response. In addition to these supporting roles, ICU technicians provide instruction for the professional DVM veterinary students, as well as Bachelor's degree Veterinary Medical Technology students. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: AHC - Emergency and Critical Care Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Provide intensive care treatment and monitoring for critically ill patients admitted to the Animal Health Center. 2. Assist and support the receiving and care of after hours emergency and referral patients. 3. Instruct, evaluate, and assist professional (DVM) veterinary students and veterinary technology (BS) students on technical health care procedures and skills. 4. Act as a senior level manager of ICU and Emergency Service in absence of faculty members or house officers, ICU technicians are responsible for case monitoring, decision making, consulting, and overall management to ensure the highest possible patient outcome. 5. Maintain all medical recordkeeping in accordance with college policy and veterinary medical accreditation standards. 6. Check, stock, clean, maintain, supply, organize, re-stock, and disinfect the ICU and SAIM areas. 7. Set-up, monitor, maintain, and use specialized diagnostic and therapeutic equipment in patient care. 8. Perform a wide range of diagnostic procedures with appropriate sample submission to the laboratory. 9. Supervise and/or administer anesthesia during diagnostic or therapeutic procedures. 10. Restrain, move, and handle animals while instructing others on appropriate techniques, protocols and treatment schedules. 11. Interact with the college's stakeholders including the general public, co-workers, students, and faculty demonstrating excellent verbal and written communication skills in a professional manner. 12. Regulate and monitor after hours access to pharmaceuticals and supplies. 13. Work various shifts as assigned and directed to provide adequate coverage (24/7/365) for the unit. 14. Perform related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Associate Degree Veterinary Medicine or Veterinary Technology Experience (yrs.): 2 years Direct Experience Applicants that adequately demonstrate the possibility of meeting the minimum requirements in terms of experience, Education: and/or program requirements within the next 12 months will be considered. The minimum requirements must be met prior to employment start date. Substitution allowed: Any equivalent combination of related experience and/or Education: approved by the Department of Human Resources Management. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Bachelors Degree 2. Certified Veterinary technician (AD)/technologist (BS) 3. Specialty Certification in Emergency and Critical Care Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies 2. Records maintenance skills. 3. Ability gather data, compile information, and prepare reports. 4. Skill in use of personal computers and related software applications. 5. Database management skills. 6. Ability to analyze and solve problems. 7. Ability to create, compose, and edit written materials. 8. Knowledge of human resources process, procedures, and documentation, as applicable to a public institution. Working Conditions and Physical Effort No unusual physical requirements. Requires some heavy lifting, and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. Routine deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, and handling objects with hands. Job occasionally requires standing, walking, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include a cover letter and resume along with names and addresses of at least three references.f Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 275423bd Last Name (required) af32c05d Email (required) c929666f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 9bfdc399 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 6ea8e78c Last Name (required) 9cae30f0 Email (required) 3d1ecf4a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-research-associate-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-30f96433-0f5b-4601-a4f7-20d00cb9a1ec": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Main Campus",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Research Associate - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Postdoctoral Research Associate - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Postdoctoral Research Associate 511375 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 192900 - nSPARC Professional Time-Limited Full-Time 12-Month Opening on: Oct 13 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The National Strategic Planning & Analysis Research Center (NSPARC) at Mississippi State University is a trusted source for inspired research, advanced analytics, and software architecture and development. NSPARC conducts interdisciplinary work across workforce and economic development, education, health, human services, corrections, and related public-interest domains. NSPARC seeks a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher to join an interdisciplinary team conducting applied research. The successful candidate will work with combinations of structured and unstructured data, including tabular and administrative records, longitudinal and time-series data, text, images, and other sensor or digital data, and translate research questions into reproducible analyses, validated models, scholarly products, and decision-support tools. The candidate will also design, develop, and evaluate artificial intelligence and machine learning methods for complex, multimodal datasets. A central expectation of the position is to work closely with NSPARC research faculty and staff to contribute to the Center’s research portfolio through the development of new research ideas, preparation of research proposals and grant applications, and writing peer-reviewed publications. The candidate will also be encouraged to explore emerging research directions, help formulate research questions, and contribute to collaborative and interdisciplinary projects. The role is well suited to a researcher who can move fluently from research question formulation and exploration analysis to model development, rigorous evaluation, interpretation, and communication. The candidate will work closely with research faculty, scientists, software engineers, data professionals, and students to conduct interdisciplinary research, and explore emerging research directions, while demonstrating initiative and intellectual independence. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Scholarly research and publication: Work with research faculty to formulate research questions, conduct rigorous and reproducible research, and contribute to peer-reviewed journal and conference publications. • Research proposal development: Support research faculty in developing competitive research proposals and grant applications, including literature reviews, problem formulation, methodological design, preliminary analyses, and preparation of technical content. • Research exploration and innovation: Explore emerging AI/ML methods, research problems, and application areas; identify promising research directions and contribute ideas that can lead to new studies, publications, and collaborative research initiatives. • Funding opportunity exploration: Identify and review relevant research funding opportunities from federal agencies such as the National Science Foundation (NSF), Department of Energy (DOE), National Institutes of Health (NIH), and other public or private sponsors; work with NSPARC research faculty to assess alignment with the Center’s research capabilities and priorities and help develop potential research directions in response to appropriate funding opportunities. • Multimodal research: Develop AI/ML approaches that integrate and analyze tabular, time-series, textual, image, and other data modalities. • Data engineering: Acquire, clean, harmonize, link, transform, document, and quality-check large and heterogeneous datasets; build reusable and auditable data pipelines. • Time-series modeling: Conduct temporal and longitudinal analyses, including forecasting, anomaly detection, sequence modeling, and appropriate validation under temporal dependence. • Computer vision: Develop and evaluate models for image classification, object detection, segmentation, representation learning, and related vision tasks. • Language and multimodal AI: Build and assess natural language processing, large language model (LLM), vision-language model (VLM), embedding, retrieval-augmented generation, and multimodal fusion workflows when appropriate to project goals. • Model evaluation: Design rigorous experiments; select meaningful baselines and metrics; assess generalization, calibration, uncertainty, robustness, bias, fairness, and error patterns. • Research translation: Convert analytical results into clear reports, visualizations, presentations, technical documentation, and actionable recommendations for technical and nontechnical audiences. • Statistical and descriptive analysis: Conduct rigorous descriptive and traditional statistical analyses, including data summarization, estimation, hypothesis testing, regression, analysis of variance, and other appropriate inferential methods; clearly interpret assumptions, effect sizes, uncertainty, and practical significance. • Collaboration: Provide comprehensive research support for interdisciplinary projects, contribute to research and project planning, data analysis, development of research reports and other deliverables, and collaborate effectively with internal and external researchers and project teams. Additional duties may be assigned consistent with the knowledge, skills, and abilities required for the position. Minimum Qualifications: A PhD in Computer Science, Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Electrical and Computer Engineering, Statistics, Applied Mathematics, or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: • Hands-on experience with PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, or comparable machine-learning frameworks. • Experience with multimodal learning, representation learning, data fusion, or joint modeling across structured data, time series, text, images, video, audio, or sensor data. • Experience developing computer vision systems using convolutional neural networks, vision transformers, vision foundation models, or related architectures. • Experience adapting, fine-tuning, evaluating, or deploying LLMs and VLMs; familiarity with prompting, embeddings, retrieval-augmented generation, parameter-efficient tuning, and multimodal evaluation. • Experience with forecasting, temporal deep learning, or longitudinal modeling. • Experience working with administrative, education, workforce, economic, health, geospatial, or other public-sector data. • A strong publication record and demonstrated ability to contribute to manuscripts, grant proposals, or sponsored research deliverables. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Demonstrated ability to formulate research questions, review and synthesize relevant literature, design rigorous experiments, and interpret research findings. • Demonstrated ability to communicate research methods and findings through scholarly manuscripts, technical reports, presentations, or other research products. • Ability to work effectively with research faculty and interdisciplinary teams in developing research ideas, conducting studies, and contributing to publications and research proposals. • Strong proficiency in Python and common ability to write clear, efficient, maintainable, and reproducible research code. • Demonstrated capability in data engineering, exploratory data analysis, feature engineering, statistical reasoning, and validation of large or complex datasets. • Working knowledge of supervised and unsupervised learning, deep learning, model selection, hyperparameter optimization, and appropriate experimental design. • Ability to work with multiple data modalities and select methods that fit the research question, data-generating process, and operational constraints. • Strong written and oral communication skills, including the ability to explain technical methods, assumptions, limitations, and results to audiences. • Ability to work independently, manage priorities and deadlines, and contribute effectively within an interdisciplinary and broad research environment. • Commitment to research integrity, responsible AI, data privacy, security, reproducibility, and ethical use of sensitive or restricted data. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Work is performed primarily in a comfortable indoor office or computing environment and frequently involves sitting, communicating, hearing, handling objects, and viewing information in print or electronically. The position requires limited lifting of files and records. Work may involve externally imposed deadlines, changing priorities, interruptions, coordination of unrelated activities, and occasional conflict-resolution or other stressful interactions. Occasional overnight travel may be expected. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants should complete the online application at explore.msujobs.msstate.edu and upload: • A cover letter describing research interests and alignment with the position; • A current curriculum vitae or résumé. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 1c794ef0 Last Name (required) 7cb1bc8e Email (required) 686dc6f1 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert a292093f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Time-Limited Full-Time 12-Month Time-Limited Full-Time 12-Month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 21e6001d Last Name (required) e44d1a10 Email (required) 483cb721 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
