    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/animal-health-technician-trainee-i-or-ii-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-772aad69-af9a-4a4f-ae06-02376664fd76": {
      "title": "Animal Health Technician Trainee, I, or II - Main Campus",
      "description": "Animal Health Technician Trainee, I, or II - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Animal Health Technician Trainee, I, or II - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Animal Health Technician Trainee, I, or II 511361 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 184100 - CVM AHC Administration Professional Part-Time 12-Month Opening on: Oct 8 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: To provide specialized nursing and technical support for veterinary oncology patients undergoing diagnostic, therapeutic, and supportive care procedures; supervise/teach students in the practice of veterinary oncology; maintain oncology equipment and treatment records; and assist clinicians in delivering comprehensive oncology care. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: AHC - Oncology Service Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Assist with the evaluation, treatment, and monitoring of oncology patients receiving chemotherapy, radiation therapy, immunotherapy, and other cancer-related treatments. • Prepare and administer chemotherapy and other oncology medications in accordance with established safety protocols and regulatory guidelines. • Monitor chemotherapy pharmacy inventory, ensure proper handling and disposal of hazardous drugs, and maintain accurate treatment records. • Set up and maintain oncology treatment areas and specialized equipment. • Monitor patients during treatments and recovery periods, recognizing and responding to adverse reactions or complications. • Collect and process laboratory samples, interpret basic laboratory data, and communicate patient status to clinicians. • Educate and support clients regarding oncology treatment plans, medication administration, home care instructions, and potential side effects. • Instruct veterinary and veterinary technician students on oncology nursing procedures, chemotherapy safety, patient handling, case management, and supportive care techniques. • Supervise and assist students during oncology procedures and patient treatments and evaluate student performance as assigned. • Maintain detailed medical records, treatment logs, chemotherapy administration records, and billing documentation. • Assist with scheduling and coordination of oncology appointments and follow-up care. • Participate in maintaining compliance with hospital safety standards and hazardous drug handling protocols. Minimum Qualifications: Trainee Level High School Diploma or Equivalent. Must possess a veterinary technology or technician degree. Must obtain certification within 1 calendar year of hire. Level I High School Diploma or Equivalent. Certification as a Veterinary Technician or Registered Nurse, plus 4 years of related experience. Level II High School Diploma or Equivalent. Certification as a Veterinary Technician or Registered Nurse, plus 4 years of related experience and 3 years’ experience as Oncology Technician I or 5 or more years’ experience in private practice or specialty practice. Rank and salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work with all kinds of animals. Working knowledge of oncology nursing care, chemotherapy administration and safety procedures, patient restraint, venipuncture, catheter placement, sedation, anesthesia monitoring, and supportive care techniques. Ability to communicate effectively with clinicians, students, staff, and clients regarding oncology treatment plans and patient care. Familiarity with hazardous drug handling procedures and oncology treatment protocols. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. Job requires standing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include a cover letter and resume along with names and addresses of at least three references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) acf997a3 Last Name (required) b0f807ed Email (required) ef530701 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 68882342 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Part-Time 12-Month Part-Time 12-Month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) d64b1465 Last Name (required) addedcf9 Email (required) f5b214e4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
