    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-f6b22e43-dbdd-4f84-8422-36cf07a642f4": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor 511250 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 036900 - Mathematics & Statistics Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Oct 7 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Department of Mathematics & Statistics at Mississippi State University invites applicants for a tenure-track appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor with an anticipated start date of Fall 2027. This role will be responsible for teaching, research, and service in Mathematics. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: See the departmental website located at www.math.msstate.edu Area of Specialization: Mathematics Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate level courses, develop a substantial research program in an area of mathematics, provide direction and effective leadership for M.S. and Ph.D. students, and engage in departmental, university and scientific community service functions. Minimum Qualifications: Successful applicants will hold a Doctoral degree, or a doctoral degree expected no later than July 2027 in Mathematics. Commitment to effective graduate and undergraduate teaching. Demonstrated success in research. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Successful applicants will hold a doctoral degree and possess the ability to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, develop a research program, mentor graduate students and engage in service functions. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Standard office and professional environment. Instructions for Applying: All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter and current curriculum vitae, including a publication list. For full consideration, please also submit a summary of research plans and teaching philosophy, a completed AMS Standard Cover Sheet (http://www.ams.org/employment) and four reference letters, one of which must address the candidate's teaching qualifications, to be submitted by the reference writers via http://www.mathjobs.org/jobs addressed to Chair, Applied Mathematics Search Committee, Department of Mathematics and Statistics, Mississippi State University, Mississippi State, MS 39762-9715. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) cc59831a Last Name (required) 49cb49df Email (required) 8dca0d91 Refer someone to this j