    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/financial-aid-counselor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-65d18b50-1338-4da3-8fef-e3ba370807e4": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Financial Aid Counselor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Financial Aid Counselor 511295 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 410600 - Financial Aid and Scholarships Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Responsible for assigned activities related to the processing and management of the Federal Direct Student Loan and Alternative Loan programs. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Provide financial aid counseling to students and parents on the financial aid programs and application processes with concentration on the Federal Direct Loan and Alternative Loan programs. 2. Review financial aid information, including electronic data and reports, to determine the loan eligibility of student applicants. 3. Award and originate Federal Direct Student loans to eligible student applicants. 4. Receive and send student loan data for processing through the data transmission systems, Edconnect and ELM. 5. Keep abreast of the state, federal, and institutional rules and regulations applicable to the administration of the student loan programs. 6. Prepare data for correspondence, including letters, emails, and other documents used to communicate with students and parents on the student loan programs. 7. Assist in the development and revision of the procedures for administering the student loan programs. 8. Participate in student orientation and financial aid presentation events. 9. Participate in staff development and financial aid training events. 10. Perform other related tasks as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Strong verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills 2. Strong analytical and organizational skills 3. Ability to learn, interpret and apply complex federal financial aid regulations 4. Ability to utilize computer skills in an automated work environment 5. Ability to provide excellent customer service Working Conditions and Physical Effort • Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. • No or very limited physical effort required. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter, current resume or curriculum vitae, and the complete contact information for at least three professional references Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 0b28e5b6 Last Name (required) 943e8d78 Email (required) 43bc9c7f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert b35695d9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 96c6c8b1 Last Name (required) 5