    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/cheesemaker-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-4515865f-1a5b-4263-9466-64fa3401a2f8": {
      "title": "Cheesemaker - Main Campus",
      "description": "Cheesemaker - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Cheesemaker - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Cheesemaker 511342 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 010208 - Custer Dairy Processing Plant Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Process raw materials to make cheese. Salary Grade : 09 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Anticipated Appointment Date: November 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Performs various test and procedures to manufacture Edam, Cheddar and other cheese products. 2. Assist in preparing hoop for cheese; fill hoop, dress cheese, and remove cheese from hoops. 3. Wax, wrap, bag and box cheese. 4. Place cheese in storage for aging. 5. Prepare starter for culture for cheese. 6. Maintain detailed and accurate records. 7. Transport raw milk from dairy to dairy processing plant. 8. Responsible for the quality and aspects of production of the cheese. 9. Provides guidance to all employees involved in the cheese making process. 10. Assist with mailing of cheese orders. 11. Assist with the manufacturing of other dairy products. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High school Diploma 1. Valid Driver's License and ability to obtain Commercial Driver’s license within 6 months of employment. 2. Once CDL is obtained, must complete drug tests which indicate an absence of illegal controlled substance use. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work with others. Good communication skills. Ability to follow instructions. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Ability to wear steel toed boots for ten (10) hours a day. 2. Frequently lift 100 pounds. 3. Ability to stoop and bend for extended periods of time. 4. Ability to lift and stack cheese in stacks up to twelve (12) feet high Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu Screening Date: October 13, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 781e502d Last Name (required) 71c7414e Email (required) aa553e37 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert fc27ce36 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 87ec2b70 Last Name (required) 2d5440a4 Email (required) 97cc3bff Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
