    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/video-producer-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Video Producer - Main Campus",
      "description": "Video Producer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Video Producer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Video Producer 511262 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011000 - Agricultural Communications Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Video Producer is a member of the Electronic Media Section in the Office of Agricultural Communications. This position creates video news and feature stories, social media video, promotional and educational project work, graphic elements, and supplementary media for MSU Extension podcast episodes. This position supports the teaching, research, and service mission of the Division of Agriculture, Forestry, and Veterinary Medicine. The Division includes six major units: the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS), the College of Forest Resources (CFR), the College of Veterinary Medicine (CVM), the Forest and Wildlife Research Center (FWRC), the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station (MAFES), and the Mississippi State University Extension Service (MSU‐ES). Salary Grade : 13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Office of Agricultural Communications provides professional communications, leadership and marketing strategies, media production, and publications management to serve the MSU Extension Service and the Division of Agriculture, Forestry, and Veterinary Medicine and select organizations. Our department specializes in educational and marketing publications, media relations, graphic design, photography, video production, social media, and premium-grade printing services. Anticipated Appointment Date: November 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The person in this position must be skilled in video production and able to develop, research, package and communicate ideas, concepts, storylines, and procedures to target audiences through visual and aural media. The position involves videography, script writing, nonlinear video editing, and narration of scripts. This position is responsible for researching, writing, and producing educational and/or promotional video materials for internal and external audiences. The successful candidate will be expected to work as an effective team member, manage multiple projects, and deliver assignments on deadline. Strong communication skills are necessary for working with MSU Extension program leaders and research specialists presenting complex subject matter. This necessitates the ability to transform technical, educational data into video productions appropriate for intended audiences. Advanced story telling capabilities are a must. The video producer must be able to operate a variety of production equipment, including but not limited to, nonlinear video editing and graphics platforms, professional 4k video cameras, on set lighting, and other related production equipment. Knowledge of agriculture and/or MSU Extension programming would be beneficial. Minimum Qualifications: Education - Bachelor's Degree with a Focus on Journalism, Communications or closely related field Experience (yrs.) One year Video production that includes writing, videography, editing with non-linear video editing systems and producing Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong writing skills appropriate for educational video production; demonstrated ability to pre-plan a field production, work independently to operate video editing platforms, use voice to communicate effectively, work well with diverse clientele, colleagues and the general public. High level production planning skills and creativity in script writing, videography, narration recording, and video and audio editing. Working Conditions and Physical Effort - Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment but may also involve outdoor work under various weather and environmental conditions and work at various locations where video footage is required. - Must be able to travel independently and be able to carry and use video production equipment including camera, tripod, audio recording equipment, light kit, and other essential equipment. - Limited exposure to physical risk. - Moderate physical effort required. - Ability to life 50-100 lbs. - Position requires frequent travel. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ To apply, please complete the online application and attach a cover letter and resume' Screening Date: October 20, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 46f8aa2c Last Name (required) faa006b2 Email (required) 6509a202 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 1b61d9a1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 79c101f3 Last Name (r