    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/eh-s-specialist-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "EH&S Specialist - Main Campus",
      "description": "EH&S Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States EH&S Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! EH&S Specialist 511346 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 493002 - Environmental Hlth & Safety Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 5 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The EH&S Specialist will administer environmental health and safety programs to provide a safe and healthy environment for our campus community. Primary duties include the day-to-day administration and coordination of the University's environmental health and safety programs in a responsive manner that provides the highest level of service to the campus community. The EH&S Specialist will ensure compliance with regulatory requirements, nationally recognized standards and university policies and procedures. The EH&S Specialist reports to the Associate Director of EH&S. This job shall be considered a generalist. but it may also specify responsibilities pertaining to professional competencies necessary for a more focused position specialization in the following safety areas 1. Biological 2. Hazardous 3. Fire Protection 4. Radiological 5. Laboratory 6. Occupational Salary Grade : 13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Manages or coordinates the development and implementation of the comprehensive environmental health and safety programs which may focus on a specialization 2. Assists faculty and staff with all matters related to safety including compliance and interpretation regarding general safety regulations and guidelines or those applicable to specialization 3. Participates in the development of general safety mitigation procedures, emergency/incident response, and safety plans or those applicable to specialization. 4. Assist with or implements general safety-relevant policies, procedures, and guidelines or those applicable to specialization. 5. Participates in the review and approval of university research protocols and operating procedures applicable to specialization. 6. Participates in planning phases of construction within the context of general safety or area of specialization 7. Conducts general inspections, certifications, and monitors faculty and staff compliance with regard to university policies, procedures, guidelines, national recognized standards, and governmental law or those applicable to specialization. 8. Participates or supports relevant University committees, task forces or working groups. 9. Completes or assist with general accident and incident resolutions through investigations, recommendation of corrective or preventive measures. and he development or implementation of programs needed to reduce or eliminate the probability of a reoccurrence or those applicable to specialization. 10. Develops, implements, and conducts general training for the campus community or those applicable to specialization 11. Shall maintain appropriate expertise on existing and proposed changes in regulations interprets and applies relevant, laws, regulations, codes and best practices, including making recommendations for work changes based on interpretations and principles of professional practices within area of specialization. 12. Performs other related duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Level 1- Bachelor's Degree in relevant field- 0 years experience Level 2- Bachelor's Degree in relevant field- 2 years experience Level 3- Bachelor's Degree in relevant field- 4 years experience Level 4-Bachelor's Degree in relevant field-6 years experiences Preferred Qualifications: Level 1- Bachelor's degree in Environmental Science, Health Safety, Industrial Hygiene, Biological Sciences, Engineering, Chemistry or a related field. 1 year experience of position-related in environmental, health, or safety field Level 2- Bachelor's degree in Environmental Science, Health Safety, Industrial Hygiene, Biological Sciences, Engineering, Chemistry or a related field. 2 year experience of position-related in environmental, health, or safety field. Associate Safety and Health Manager, Certified Safety Manager, Licensed Safety Professional, or other related certifications. Level 3- Bachelor's degree in Environmental Science, Health Safety, Industrial Hygiene, Biological Sciences, Engineering, Chemistry or a related field. 4 years experience of position-related in environmental, health, or safety field. Certified Safety Manager, Graduate Safety Professional, Certified Safety Professional or other related certification Level 4- Bachelor's degree in Environmental Science, Health Safety, Industrial Hygiene, Biological Sciences, Engineering, Chemistry or a related field. 6 year experience of position-related in environmental, health, or safety field. Certified Safety Professional, Certified Industrial Hygienist, or other related certifications. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Demonstrate excellent communication and organizational skills 2. Possess an understanding of relevant federal laws and guidelines. 3. Be willing to travel to obtain continuing education 4. Able to work independently with minimal direct supervision 5. Demonstrate self-motivation and attention to detail 6. Able to work in a team environment and foster cooperative relationships within MSU and within the community. 7. Able to review goals, analyze processes and develop approaches required to meet objectives 8. Familiar with database and website systems Working Conditions and Physical Effort The position may require work with hazardous materials or be in areas where radiation producing equipment, radioactive materials, chemicals, or infectious agents are present, wearing personal protective equipment and respirator in certain circumstances may be required. Physical requirements include frequent sitting, talking, hearing, walking, and standing. Occasionally requires reaching, climbing or balancing, stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, handling objects with hands and lifting up to ten pounds. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) e9cfb8e8 Last Name (required) 55037f28 Email (required) 75b6b974 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 7844f537 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) bccc715d Last Name (required) 13e7a537 Email (required) 2ae262f2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
