    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/extension-research-associate-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-b2fc4c62-44d3-4d3d-859d-bba4a26e9ca5": {
      "title": "Extension/Research Associate - Main Campus",
      "description": "Extension/Research Associate - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Extension/Research Associate - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Extension/Research Associate 511293 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011100 - Plant and Soil Sciences Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 1 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: This is a full-time Extension Research Associate position that will provide technical and managerial assistance in daily operations and long-term planning of the Peanut Extension program. The overall objectives of this position are to assist the program in providing knowledge to the peanut stakeholders of Mississippi, develop new scientific knowledge to the peanut scientific community, and assisting student employees/graduate students. Salary Grade : 13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Mississippi State is Mississippi's senior comprehensive land-grant institution and has the largest on-campus enrollment (>22,000) of the eight state institutions of higher learning. All components of the university have a strong commitment to teaching, research, and service. The Department of Plant and Soil Sciences has 33 on- and 14 off-campus faculty members engaged in teaching, research, and extension and/or service programs, most of whom carry joint appointments. The programs are supported by state-of-the-art, newly renovated laboratories, equipment, and trained support and professional staff. The department offers Bachelor of Science degrees in Plant and Soil Sciences with Master's and Doctoral graduate students concentrating in Agronomy and, Horticulture. Area of Specialization: Peanut Anticipated Appointment Date: November 1, 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Manage field research/demonstration plots at multiple locations across the state. This includes the operation and hauling of farm equipment, data collection, and crop management. 2. Supervision of student employees and assisting graduate students with field research projects. 3. Monitoring/purchasing of agronomic and research supplies. Seasonal farm equipment and vehicle maintenance. 4. Assisting with field days, grower meetings, and other activities, which may include public speaking. 5. Present research at scientific conferences. 6. Data analysis to prepare scientific and commodity board reports. 7. Performs miscellaneous job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in related field. Rank and salary will be commensurate with education/experience of the candidate. Preferred Qualifications: Experience operating farm machinery. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Applicant must have excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent organizational and leadership skills are also imperative.The applicant must possess strong leadership, organization, and communication skills. The applicant must be capable of completing detail oriented task and deliver high quality work. Motivation to learn and continue professional development is necessary Working Conditions and Physical Effort Exposure to educational and agricultural conditions. Lifting, sitting, standing, squatting, etc. will be required. Exposure to chemicals, dust, heat, and cold. Additional exposures may be encountered in a lab setting. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu 1. Resume or curriculum vitae. 2. Brief cover letter (1-page) outlining your qualifications and position interest. 3. College transcripts. Any social security numbers on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online. 4. Names and contact information of three professional references. Screening Date: October 15, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2ac900d6 Last Name (required) d2d5ef80 Email (required) fe47d1fa Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 70e4cc2c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 93a37f93 Last Name (required) b6adda39 Email (required) 1888286b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
