    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/meat-laboratory-associate-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Meat Laboratory Associate - Main Campus",
      "description": "Meat Laboratory Associate - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Meat Laboratory Associate - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Meat Laboratory Associate 511287 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011300 - Animal & Dairy Science Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 1 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The successful candidate will be responsible for assisting in all aspects of the Meat Science and Muscle Biology laboratory management. This includes harvest, fabrication, processing, distribution, and retailing of meat products, as well as sanitation and supply inventory, while adhering to all USDA regulations. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Animal and Dairy Sciences is currently seeking a Meat Laboratory Associate to assist in the research management and production operations of the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station (MAFES) Meat Science and Muscle Biology Laboratory. The Meat Science and Muscle Biology Laboratory is a 15,000 sq. ft. state-of-the-art processing facility. Anticipated Appointment Date: October 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Responsibilities include but are not limited to: 1. Harvest, fabrication, processing, distribution, and retailing of meat products. 2. Assist with research projects and teaching activities. 3. Fulfill USDA (FSIS) inspection, HACCP, and SSOP requirements. 4. Assist in the training and supervision of undergraduate and graduate students. 5. Maintain a safe and clean facility. 6. Operation and maintenance of specialized equipment. Multiple Units on campus utilize the Meat Science and Muscle Biology Laboratory. The successful candidate will be expected to work with faculty from all Departments. In addition to the job requirements listed above, the successful candidate will have the opportunity to explore an advanced degree. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High School Diploma or GED Substitution allowed: An equivalent combination of related education and related experience may be considered for this position. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Animal and Dairy Science or a closely related field. Preference will be given to a candidate with meat laboratory management or meats judging experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of all aspects of butchery including, but not limited to, harvest, fabrication, retail merchandising, further processing and cooking. Must have knowledge of USDA regulations regarding meat processing establishments and comprehensive experience in HACCP, GMPs, SSOPS, Pest Control, and Biosecurity. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Frequent heavy or intense physical requirements may be required. The position has routine deadlines; usually, sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than the immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires standing, walking, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands, and lifting up to 25 pounds. Job occasionally requires sitting, climbing, or balancing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/ crawling, and lifting more than 100 pounds. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants MUST complete the online application located at www.jobs.msstate.edu to be considered for this position. A cover letter, resume, academic transcripts (with any social security numbers redacted), and contact information for three references should be submitted with the application. Screening Date: October 8, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f7d7b46c Last Name (required) b057359c Email (required) 47b93079 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 63428517 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 9ff5c102 Last Name (required) 2c6b3e62 Email (required) a789f704 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
