    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/admissions-coordinator-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Admissions Coordinator - Main Campus",
      "description": "Admissions Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Admissions Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Admissions Coordinator 511315 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 088801 - Colg of Forest Resources-Dean Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The CFR Admissions Coordinator serves under the administrative supervision of the Director (or Assistant Dean) of Student Recruitment and Retention. Primary roles of the position are to: • Recruit undergraduate students to the College of Forest Resources • Coordinate and assist with academic activities and events for the College of Forest Resources • Develop and implement strategies to recruit scholarly students to the College of Forest Resources. • Develop and implement strategies to grow enrollment in majors with high job demand and placement. Salary Grade : 14 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Admissions Coordinator will serve the College of Forest Resources (CFR) at Mississippi State University. The mission of CFR is to foster the management, conservation, and sustainable use of forest, wildlife, and aquatic resources to benefit the people of Mississippi, the nation, and the world. CFR offers 4 majors and 16 concentrations and hundreds of careers. CFR provides students with ample opportunities to join discipline-oriented clubs and organizations and engage in undergraduate research. Anticipated Appointment Date: November 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Coordinate off-campus recruiting and assist with on-campus recruiting which includes, but is not limited to the following: a. College Fairs b. Private Visits c. Classroom Workshops d. On-campus after-school and summer programs 2. Lead CFR Academic Insight and Awards Banquet 3. Collaborate with campus-wide partners in the College of Forest Resources, Office of Admissions and Scholarships, Housing and Residence Life, Financial Aid and the broader MSU campus 4. Maintain relationships with high schools, academies, community colleges and the CFR Community Partner Network. 5. Travel to recruiting events and sites to meet with students, parents and stakeholders 6. Address and refer inquires and informational requests from faculty, students, and parents or guardians 7. Coordinate campus visits with prospective students and parents or guardians 8. Maintain prospective student contact files and databases 9. Recruit, manage and mentor the CFR Student Ambassadors 10. Coordinate and assist with student orientation sessions 11. Collaborate with Marketing Director to maintain and develop CFR recruiting materials 12. Coordinate recruiting communication plan 13. Collaborate with the Director (or Assistant Dean) of Student Recruitment and Retention to develop and manage annual recruitment budget 14. Chair the CFR Recruitment Committee, and serve as a liaison for CFR on the University Recruitment Council 15. Other responsibilities deemed appropriate Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Natural Resources, Student Affairs, or other degrees related to this position. Valid driver's license. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with students, parents or guardians, academic administrators, and faculty. University level recruiting experience and demonstrated success. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Excellent communication and interpersonal skills • Strong organizational and multitasking skills • Proficiency in using relevant software and databases • Strong public speaking and presentation skills • Ability to travel for recruitment events and activities • Demonstrated ability to work independently and as part of a team • Strong customer service skills • Well developed written and verbal skills • Ability to make data driven decisions Working Conditions and Physical Effort No unusual physical requirements. Nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. Routine deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires sitting, handling objects with hands. Job requires substantial travel, involving overnight stays, to perform recruiting duties and attend events Job occasionally requires standing, walking, reaching, talking, hearing, and lifting up to 30 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must submit their application at https://www.msujobs.msstate.edu/ and attach 1) a cover letter, 2) current resume, 3) the complete contact information for three professional references, and 4) a copy of transcripts with any social security numbers redacted before upload. Official transcripts are required upon employment. Screening Date: October 14, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) de2cdc91 Last Name (required) 713c98f3 Email (required) f77c5345 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 1311a235 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) fd611b87 Last Name (required) 64f29e23 Email (required) 75c4f4c9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
