    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/extension-project-specialist-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-ab2a5a85-5d99-4a23-8d2c-417d619e4897": {
      "title": "Extension Project Specialist - Main Campus",
      "description": "Extension Project Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Extension Project Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Extension Project Specialist 511313 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011400 - Extension Center for Tech Outreach Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: In the Extension Center for Technology Outreach, the Extension Project Specialist will provide hardware, software, and user support to meet CTO client needs in the area of video conferencing, audio/video technologies, video recording/editing and will provide maintenance, repair, upkeep and support for computers and other electronics both in the unit and in all supported units. The Extension Project Specialist should use advanced learning technologies such as online training modules and courses, webinars, video conferencing to reach Extension audiences and other Extension employees. Salary Grade : 15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Anticipated Appointment Date: November 1, 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Provide technical support and training on a variety of video recording, conferencing, audiovisual equipment hardware and software. 2. Install and maintain networking infrastructure needed to support video conferencing systems including endpoints, LAN, and WAN components utilized by all supported units. 3. Extensive working knowledge of Microsoft operating systems and Windows 11. 4. Knowledge of a broad range of software tools including Microsoft Office. 5. Design and implement programming of control systems in video conferencing rooms. 6. Provide video recording and editing support to other Extension personnel. 7. Produce and edit videos. 8. Experience using Adobe Creative Cloud applications, including Premiere Pro, After Effects, Photoshop, Audition, and Acrobat, for video production, graphic design, document creation, and multimedia content development. 9. Work and support the mission of all program areas in the Extension Service including Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family, Health, and Wellness, 4-H, and Government and Community Development. 10. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: - Bachelor's degree in an area related to Technology, Management/Business Information Systems, Agriculture Information Science and Education, or other related fields and 3 years of experience. OR -Master's Degree in an area related to Technology, Management/Business Information Systems, Agriculture Information Science and Education, or other related fields, plus one year experience. Indicated education is required; no substitutions allowed. Rank and Salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Knowledge and experience with repair of multiple types of electronic devices including video cameras, video recorders/servers/storage devices, desktop/notebook computers, printers, monitors, peripheral devices, and networking electronics. 2. Experience and understanding of using various technology education methods for both in-person and distance education. 3. Experience and understanding of webinars, videoconferencing, development of online training modules. 4. Strong analytical and technical skills with an attention for detail and accuracy. 5. Skilled in working with video editing software. 6. Highly self-motivated and directed, with experience working both independently and, in a team,-oriented, collaborative environment. Working Conditions and Physical Effort - Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. - No or very limited exposure to physical risk. - Some physical effort required including lifting up to 50 pounds. - Some in-state and out-of-state travel may be required. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu and submit a resume, cover letter, unofficial transcript (with social security numbers redacted) and contact information for three references. Screening Date: October 14, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) aad55468 Last Name (required) 45f7fc1e Email (required) 67a44f1c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert c931c77f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 5cc511b4 Last Name (required) 2910f744 Email (required) e0a57f02 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
