      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Teaching Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Teaching Professor 511204 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 038600 - Psychology Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Sep 29 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Department of Psychology at Mississippi State University is seeking applications for a nine-month, non-tenure track faculty position as an Assistant Teaching Professor starting in August 2027. A doctorate in Psychology or related science discipline is required. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Psychology is within the College of Arts & Sciences. It houses 25 full-time faculty members, over 800 undergraduates, and about 45 doctoral students in our Cognitive Science and Clinical Psychology Ph.D. programs. Area of Specialization: Psychology Anticipated Appointment Date: August 16, 2027 Tenure Track Status: Non-Tenure Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in psychology with a focus on our undergraduate Distance Education program. Candidates should have a high commitment to quality teaching at the undergraduate, and potentially graduate, level. The successful candidate will also have service involvement in the Department of Psychology including coordinating aspects of our Distance program. Minimum Qualifications: Record of effective teaching at the college or university level Ph.D. in Psychology or closely related discipline Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ph.D. in Psychology or closely related discipline Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. 2. No or very limited exposure to physical risk. 3. No or very limited physical effort required. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter, current curriculum vitae, and the complete contact information for at least three professional references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 1094f2e1 Last Name (required) 6f5fea25 Email (required) 766d9c93 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 260a8c52 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) a6444d50 Last Name (required) 825c415d Email (required) 400e2e83 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
