    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/quality-and-safety-manager-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Quality and Safety Manager - Main Campus",
      "description": "Quality and Safety Manager - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Quality and Safety Manager - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Quality and Safety Manager 511316 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 194100 - Advanced Composites Institute Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 28 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Quality and Safety Manager is responsible for leading a comprehensive Quality Management System and site safety program for the MSU Advanced Composites Institute. This position serves as the organization's AS9100 Management Representative and is responsible for ensuring compliance with AS9100 standards, customer requirements, university policies, applicable regulatory requirements, and industry best practices. The Quality and Safety Manager develops, administers, and continuously improves quality assurance processes, internal audit programs, corrective and preventive action systems, document control procedures, and nonconformance management activities. The position serves as the primary coordinator for certification audits, customer audits, management reviews, and quality performance reporting. In addition, the position serves as ACI's Safety Manager and is responsible for developing and maintaining a safe working environment through implementation of safety policies, training programs, hazard assessments, incident investigations, risk mitigation activities, and regulatory compliance efforts. Salary Grade : 15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Advanced Composites Institute, or ACI, focuses on pioneering transformational composite technologies in a variety of critical sectors, including aerospace, civil, military, energy, automotive and other emerging markets. It was created at MSU with the donation of a revolutionary stitched composite process and equipment originally developed at NASA by pioneering scientist Marvin B. Dow. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Establish and develop programs that meet compliance with regulatory expectations for quality, yielding ISO9001 and AS9100 Certifications as well as implement and maintain safety policies and procedures that comply with local, state and federal Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) rules and regulations. 2. Serve as ISO9001 and AS9100 Management Representative: ensure that processes needed for the Quality Management System are established, implemented and maintained, report on the performance of the Quality Management System, ensure the promotion of awareness of customer requirements throughout the organization. 3. Develop, plan, implement and conduct preventive care, safety, and compliance training; and training programs on topics such as inspection techniques and proper documentation. 4. Evaluate production methods and recommend improvements based on standards that guarantee work is performed in accordance with approved manuals, internal policies and procedures, contract documents, and good engineering practices. 5. Attend regular Operations meetings to discuss QA/QC issues and provide support as needed; and conduct regular safety meetings, audits (including the facilitation of customer audits), and inspections to ensure compliance, evaluate performance, identify corrective action, and implement follow up assessments. 6. Develop sampling plans, quality standards, and process control instructions for use by Operations to monitor and reduce variations. 7. Ensure compliance with all environmental health and safety and regulatory requirements. 8. Collaborate with management to develop an Emergency Action Plan and serve as primary contact for project site injury and incident notification, investigation, and case management. 9. Responsible for electronic document management that include safety inspections, reports, violations, corrective actions, and correspondence, quality documentation (procedures, policies, audit findings, updates, etc.) 10. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility Position requires collaborative interaction at all levels of organization to expedite timely targets. The above essential duties are representative of major duties in this position. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Other duties may be assigned to the above consistent with the knowledge, skills and abilities required for the job. Not all of the duties may be assigned to a position. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Education: Bachelor’s Degree Experience (yrs.) 3 years related work experience in manufacturing technology work environment Preferred Qualifications: 1. 3 years or greater experience in aerospace manufacturing. 2. Experience working with regulatory agencies. 3. 3 years or greater experience leading cross-functional teams in a manufacturing environment to successfully accomplish safety and quality objectives. 4. Experience with QMS (Quality Management System) and AS9100. 5. Experience with data analytics. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Knowledge of quality and safety in a manufacturing work environment to successfully manage interests of all stakeholders while maximizing efforts for improving quality and safety. 2. Knowledge of customer service principles, techniques, systems, and standards. 3. Proficient communication skills to lead and engage cross-functional teams, including customers, to identify and permanently solve problems. 4. Ability to perform root cause analysis and make effective recommendation for correction. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Lifting required up to 50 pounds. Limited exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc., none to the point of being disagreeable. May involve minor safety hazards where likely result would be cuts, bruises, etc. 2. Work hours are usually between core hours of 8 am to 5 pm; workload may dictate priorities that involve occasional demands outside core work hours. 3. Job frequently requires sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands, standing, walking; job occasionally require stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, and lifting up to 50 pounds. 4. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online submitting a cover letter and resume. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f56fb0a9 Last Name (required) 7f2c5401 Email (required) 15abdeaa Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 1229331b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) b24f8408 Last Name (required) fb65c49a Email (required) ca32e7ac Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
