    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-associate-professor-or-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-57a3c1ec-2875-4a64-9c12-fda9b3509e2a": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor 511179 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 061300 - Industrial and Systems Engineering Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Sep 10 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor reports to the Head of the Department of Industrial and Systems Engineering. This is a tenure-track faculty position. The successful candidate will be an engineer and scholar with a strong commitment to teaching and conducting externally funded research. The faculty member will contribute to the University’s three primary missions of teaching, research, and service. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Industrial & Systems Engineering (ISE) Department (https://www.ise.msstate.edu/), established in 1962, is one of the eight academic departments in the James Worth Bagley College of Engineering. The ISE department is currently ranked 25th among all ISE programs nationally in research and development expenditures according to the National Science Foundation’s (NSF) HERD ranking. The department offers an ABET-accredited bachelor’s program in Industrial & Systems Engineering at the Starkville, Engineering on the Coast, and online, as well as master's and doctoral degrees at the Starkville campus and online. Current department enrollment across the three locations is 291 undergraduate students, 63 master's students, and 84 doctoral students. The department is currently supported by ten tenured/tenure-track faculty, three teaching-track faculty, one instructor, and four staff. Research expenditures totaled approximately $9 million in 2024. Area of Specialization: Industrial and Systems Engineering Department Anticipated Appointment Date: August 16, 2027 Tenure Track Status: Tenure-Track Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The following examples illustrate the types of duties assigned to this position. The absence of a specific duty does not exclude it from the position if the work is a logical assignment of the position. 1. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Industrial and Systems Engineering and serve as a research and project advisor to students at all levels. 2. Serve as an academic advisor to undergraduate and graduate students. 3. Advance the knowledge base of Industrial and Systems Engineering through research. 4. Supervise graduate student research. 5. Develop and sustain a strong, externally funded research program. 6. Publish the results of independent and sponsored research in peer-reviewed archival journals. 7. Provide service to the Department, College, and University. 8. Engage in scholarly and professional activities that maintain expertise and leadership in Industrial and Systems Engineering. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in Industrial Engineering or a closely related field is required. Candidates must demonstrate excellent interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with the candidate’s qualifications and experience. Preferred Qualifications: Professional registration, or the ability to obtain professional registration, is preferred. Previous teaching experience is also preferred. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Other qualifications include strong leadership and interpersonal skills, excellent written and verbal communication skills, and the ability to work effectively in a collaborative research environment. Successful candidates will be appointed to an academic-year position within the tenure system, with tenure considered as appropriate based on qualifications and experience. Candidates are also expected to enhance the reputation of Mississippi State University through their scholarly, professional, and service activities. Working Conditions and Physical Effort No unusual physical requirements are associated with this position. The role requires no heavy lifting, and most work is performed in a comfortable indoor environment. Instructions for Applying: Applicants must apply through Mississippi State University’s online employment system at http://www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Applicants must attach a cover letter, curriculum vitae, teaching statement, research statement, and the names, addresses, and telephone numbers of three references. Screening of applications will begin October 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 1215ba65 Last Name (required) d4d4362a Email (required) bab44d3c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert dd568820 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) ef05d3f5 Last Name (required) d1c4d07a Email (required) 8d414794 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some 