    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/engineering-shop-manager-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Engineering Shop Manager - Main Campus",
      "description": "Engineering Shop Manager - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Engineering Shop Manager - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Engineering Shop Manager 510943 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 010300 - Ag & Bio Engineering Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The individual filling this position will be responsible for coordination of labor and activities in the ABE Machine Shop, ensuring good organization and safety. The individual will work with researchers’ conceptual designs and provide practical design and construction. The individual will oversee other workspaces belonging to ABE. The individual will also be involved in teaching and overseeing students in the use of shop machines. Salary Grade : 15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Agricultural and Biological Engineering has 19 on-campus faculty members engaged in teaching, research, and extension, as well as several other faculty members at MSU-affiliated research centers and adjuncts employed elsewhere. The department is co-administered by the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences and the Bagley College of Engineering, and it offers undergraduate (B.S.) and graduate (M.S. and Ph.D.) degrees in three distinct program areas: Biomedical Engineering and Bio systems Engineering, which are both accredited by ABET, and Agricultural Engineering Technology and Business. Within these programs, the department has over 400 undergraduates and 40 graduate students. The J. Charles Lee Agricultural and Biological Engineering Building includes more than 6,000 square feet of state-of-the-art instructional and research facilities, and it includes separate labs for sterile tissue culture, bio mechanical testing, environmental and agricultural simulation or modeling studies, electronic/robotic design fabrication and testing, GPS/GIS, renewable bio energy, and student computing resources. More information about ABE can be found at http://www.abe.msstate.edu/ Anticipated Appointment Date: September 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Oversee shop operations and projects (to include labor management, machining, welding and fabrication operations, job scheduling and invoicing, and machinery maintenance). 2. Serve as building operator for the J. Charles Lee Agricultural and Biological Engineering (ABE) Building, the ABE North Farm Storage Building, and the portion of the Pace Seed Technology Laboratory Building (Pace) that the ABE Department controls. 3. Operate and maintain machine shop equipment/tools such as lathes, CNC machines, milling machines, welders, fitting machines, and woodworking machines at the journeyman level. 4. Demonstrate and provide instruction on safe operating practices and rules for the shop/laboratory. 5. Assist with design of equipment, instruments, devices, components, and systems. 6. Perform shop and laboratories duties in the ABE Department. 7. Prepare material requirement lists, order/receive materials, supplies and equipment; maintain custody and accounting records and prepare/process necessary paperwork related to cost of and securing materials, supplies, and property. 8. Assemble, construct, install/set up, and test simple or standard equipment, systems, and instruments following specific instructions from oral or written drawings/plans. These systems will include a combination of mechanical, hydraulic, pneumatic and/or electrical equipment components and controls. 9. Service/repair, adjust and/or qualify simple, standard instruments, equipment and systems on both a scheduled or recurring basis following standard work methods and using common equipment and tools. 10. Regularly review and inspect ABE and Pace facilities. 11. Occasionally work with contractors to oversee bidding and contract performance on building and renovation projects in ABE and Pace buildings. 12. Oversee and maintain ABE’s vehicle fleet (to include monthly fuel and maintenance logs and scheduled service intervals). 13. Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree. Experience: Three (3) years’ experience similar to duties described above. Licensure: Valid driver’s license. Substitution: An equivalent combination of related education and related experience may be considered for this position. Preferred Qualifications: Commercial Driver's License (CDL) Experience in hot and cold metal working, machining, and fabrication (to include SMAW, MIG and TIG welding, manual lathe and milling machine operation, and structural steel and sheet-metal layout and fabrication). Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Excellent organizational and communication skills. 2. Ability to operate, maintain and modify farm equipment (tractors, combines, sprayers, planters, etc.) 3. Ability to work with and instruct students and others in the operation and use of shop/laboratory equipment and setting up and implementing individual experiments and projects. 4. Technical experience using mechanical, electrical, and hydraulic skills. 5. Basic computer literacy and ability to use Microsoft Office suite. Working Conditions and Physical Effort * Regularly involves lifting, bending, or other physical exertion. Often exposed to one of more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. * Job frequently requires sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, and handling objects with hands. * Job occasionally requires standing, walking, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 50 pounds (e.g. fertilizer and seed, structural steel, tools, etc.) * Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online with resume, cover letter and references. Screening Date: September 10, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) cb5d802e Last Name (required) d114c917 Email (required) 5171ed0c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert f9ed03f1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 20e54fab Last Name (required) 50b86554 Email (required) 020c7ee3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
