    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/animal-care-assistant-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-ef1fa0aa-6f1a-4360-8ecc-9eeaf86dbf23": {
      "title": "Animal Care Assistant - Main Campus",
      "description": "Animal Care Assistant - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Animal Care Assistant - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Animal Care Assistant 511309 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 184100 - CVM AHC Administration Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 25 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Responsible for providing daily care, cleanliness, and upkeep for a variety of laboratory animals in a laboratory or hospital setting. Position reports to Office Manager (functional supervisor) and Technicians on duty (line managers) Salary Grade : 08 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: Animal Health Center Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Ensures animal cages and/or containment rooms are kept clean and orderly. 2. May perform a variety of animal care duties such as (but not limited to) feeding, watering, and applying shredded paper to cages. 3. The assistant is primarily responsible for cleanliness of the hospital and for assisting technicians with patient restraint. Specific Duties: • Sweep and mop the floor at least once during each shift. • Mix chemicals for cleaning according to label directions. • Clean up messes as they occur. • Empty trash as needed. Put garbage in dumpster. • Restock hospital supplies such as pill vials, syringes, bandage materials and IV supplies. • Assist with unpacking hospital supply shipments and putting items in the proper storage locations. Break down and dispose of boxes from shipments. • Keep tables, x-ray machine, CT and counters, clean, dusted, disinfected and free of debris. • Keep hospital laundry washed and dried, including surgery shrouds, towels, etc. • Keep the bathrooms cleaned and disinfected. • Replace blown light bulbs. • Keep the grounds picked up and free of litter or trash. • Keep all doors, internal windows and mirrors cleaned and smudge free. • Keep lower outside windows clean. • Spray any wasp nests as they are found. • Help properly identify and prepare cadavers for pick up. • Provide patient restraint for exam, imaging or procedures, as needed. • Run errands for the hospital. • Walk dogs outside. • Clean and disinfect kennels and runs and keep animals in a clean, sanitary and comfortable environment. • Follow all safety rules concerning animal restraint, handling cleaning supplies, and radiation safety. • Attend hospital meetings or events, when invited. • Water bushes outside, as needed. • Help with triage, including retrieving sick or injured patients from vehicles. • Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High school or equivalent. 2. Experience in animal care practices. Preferred Qualifications: N/A Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Must be neat and organized and have a strong attention to detail. Must be able to follow instructions and be good at prioritizing work in order to keep the facility, grounds and equipment clean, while at the same time helping as needed with animal restraint. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Must effectively be able to read, speak and write in English. Must be able to lift 50 lbs., work on feet all day, and handle animals up to 100 lbs. Must be punctual and able to work assigned shifts, including nights, holidays and weekends. Must follow practice dress code and present a clean and professional appearance. Must practice good hygiene minimize disease spread when handling patients. Must understand basic safety guidelines for radiation, handling cleaning chemicals and supplies, and animal restraint. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include a cover letter and resume along with names and addresses of at least three references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) c93646f9 Last Name (required) a1206f7c Email (required) ee027a67 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 018c33cf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) a40b4837 Last Name (required) 609a365b Email (required) e95d1d27 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
