    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/sentinel-landscape-program-manager-fwrc-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Sentinel Landscape Program Manager, FWRC - Main Campus",
      "description": "Sentinel Landscape Program Manager, FWRC - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Sentinel Landscape Program Manager, FWRC - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Sentinel Landscape Program Manager, FWRC 511303 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 088800 - FWRC - Director Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 24 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Sentinel Landscape Program Manager (Sentinel Landscape Coordinator) serves as the primary point of contact for the partnership and is responsible for building trusted relationships among federal, state, local, academic, nonprofit, industry, Tribal, and private landowner partners. Working under the direction of the EMSL Leadership Team, the Coordinator will facilitate collaboration, align resources, support implementation of landscape priorities, pursue funding opportunities, and measure the partnership's performance and impact. The Coordinator will foster strong connections and clear communication across local, state, regional, and federal partners, to support military readiness and local communities’ needs where interest and priorities align. Support partner success, drive implementation of shared conservation, land-use, and community goals. The position requires a collaborative leader who is highly organized, mission-focused, and capable of navigating complex partnerships while maintaining trust with agencies, landowners, elected officials, military installations, and community stakeholders. Salary Grade : 17 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The East Mississippi Sentinel Landscape (EMSL) has officially been selected for designation by the federal Sentinel Landscapes Partnership (SLP), recognizing the region’s national importance to military readiness, working lands conservation, and long-term landscape resilience. The EMSL protects nationally critical pilot training missions while also strengthening working lands, conservation efforts, outdoor recreation, and rural way of life. The Sentinel Landscape Program Manager (Sentinel Landscape Coordinator) serves as the principal coordinator and facilitator of the EMSL, providing leadership for the development and implementation of the EMSL Five-Year Implementation Plan and advancing the shared priorities of military readiness, working lands conservation, ecosystem restoration, and rural economic resilience. The Coordinator will be an employee of the Forest and Wildlife Research Center (FWRC) at Mississippi State University (MSU). The mission of FWRC is to expand through research the fundamental and applied knowledge upon which forestry, forest products, and wildlife and fisheries disciplines are based. FWRC aims to assist in conserving, developing, and using the forest, forest products, wildlife and fisheries resources of Mississippi and the nation through research, technology transfer, and other service activities. The Sentinel Landscapes Partnership is a coalition of federal agencies, state and local governments, and private organizations that work with landowners and land managers to advance sustainable land use practices around military installations and ranges. The partnership aligns the objectives of the U.S. Department of Agriculture, Department of the Interior, and Department of War to strengthen military readiness, conserve natural resources, bolster agricultural and forestry economies, increase public access to outdoor recreation, and enhance landscape resilience. Anticipated Appointment Date: October 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Foster trust, connectedness, relationships, strong networks, and partnerships across federal, state, local, and non-governmental organizations, as well as private landowners. 2. Support the EMSL Leadership Team in governance, decision-making, strategic planning, and implementation. 3. Build capacity and support the development of a steering committee and partner working groups. 4. Catalyze collective action and investment in landscape priorities by translating goals into measurable strategies and actions. 5. Lead collaborative data sharing to assess and share impacts, and enable informed decision-making across the partnership. 6. Convene and facilitate regular Steering Committee and partnership meetings, managing agendas and ensuring effective communication and task management 7. Ensure alignment with administration priorities 8. Foster collaboration and consensus among diverse stakeholders while maintaining focus on shared landscape goals. 9. Lead development, implementation, and annual updates of the EMSL Five-Year Implementation Plan, including: a. Annual work plans b. Landscape performance targets c. Acreage goals d. Assignment of lead partners e. Funding strategies f. Shared performance metrics g. Governance procedures h. Conflict-resolution processes 10. Coordinate implementation activities across all EMSL goals and support adaptive management through continuous evaluation and partner feedback. 11. Identify, pursue, and coordinate funding opportunities that support EMSL priorities. 12. Coordinate efforts supporting military readiness through compatible land use planning. 13. Coordinate implementation of landscape-scale conservation priorities. 14. Coordinate implementation with the Mississippi State Wildlife Action Plan, SECAS Blueprint, and other regional conservation initiatives. 15. Develop, collect, and report metrics demonstrating the return on investment of EMSL coordination and produce annual reports documenting progress toward military readiness, conservation, working lands, and economic resilience objectives. 16. Prepare reports, briefings, presentations, and communications for EMSL Leadership Team and partners. Minimum Qualifications: • Bachelor's degree in natural resources, forestry, wildlife, agriculture, environmental planning, public administration, military/community planning, or related field. • 5 years of experience relevant to duties described above. Preferred Qualifications: • Master's degree in a related discipline. • Experience with REPI, OLDCC, USDA conservation programs, or Sentinel Landscapes. • Knowledge of military land-use compatibility and aviation operations. • Experience with forestry, prescribed fire, watershed restoration, or working lands. • GIS literacy or experience coordinating geospatial initiatives. • Knowledge of Mississippi's agricultural, forestry, and natural resource sectors. • Experience administering grants and cooperative agreements. • Demonstrated success preparing grant applications, strategic plans, technical reports, or public presentations. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Ability to communicate effectively. 2. Knowledge of word processing and spread sheet programs. 3. Excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills required. 4. Experience coordinating multi-agency partnerships or collaborative initiatives. 5. Strong project management and organizational skills. 6. Excellent written, verbal, and public communication skills. 7. Ability to facilitate meetings and build consensus among diverse stakeholders. 8. Ability to work effectively with private landowners and rural communities. 9. Commitment to voluntary, incentive-based conservation. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. 2. No or very limited exposure to physical risk. 3. No or very limited physical effort required. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Complete the online application, include a cover letter of interest, curriculum vitae/resume (including statement of current position and responsibilities), academic transcripts with redacted SSN, include in your cover letter a statement of values, skills, and relevant experience for this position. Please provide names and contact information of three professional references. Screening Date: October 8, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 57f02efa Last Name (required) 9be7bcc7 Email (required) 307601f8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 1ebe9700 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) b7bf8741 Last Name (required) e51b72a0 Email (required) 759fe8b3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
