    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/research-engineer-i-ii-iii-or-senior-madison-county-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Engineer I, II, III or Senior",
      "description": "Research Engineer I, II, III or Senior - Madison County, Mississippi, United States Research Engineer I, II, III or Senior - Madison County, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Engineer I, II, III or Senior 511122 Madison County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 193602 - CAVS Extension Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: As a Research Engineer I, II, III, or Senior, you will play a crucial role in the support of Mississippi manufacturers and public-sector partners by assisting companies with the assessment, design, implementation, and maintenance of automation systems that improve productivity, quality, and safety. This position plays a key role in advancing economic development and innovation across the state through hands-on engineering support, applied research, and professional development initiatives. Must be a U.S. Citizen or Permanent Resident. Salary Grade : 15 This range of potential salary grades for this job positing are 15, 16, 17, and 18. Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Center for Advanced Vehicular Systems Extension (CAVS-E), headquartered in Canton, MS, maintains a strong interaction with industry and is focused on providing engineering services to manufacturing-based industries. Major activities include teaching professional development workshops, conducting on-site projects and technology transfer. The Center's ultimate objective is to assist the state in technology based economic development through projects and training with MS companies. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Perform technical assistance activities in support of industrial clients, and other key public-sector stakeholders to support expanding economic development activities within the state and region, sometimes requiring overnight stays. 2. Apply mechanical engineering principles to advanced manufacturing challenges, including production systems, equipment specification, process improvement, tooling, ergonomics, reliability, and manufacturability. 3. Support assessment, selection, implementation, and optimization of manufacturing technologies, including automation-enabled systems, data-enabled operations, and other emerging technologies. 4. Lead or support industry projects from scoping through completion, including technical planning, project scheduling, budget awareness, customer communication, documentation, and deliverables. 5. Collaborate with manufacturers to identify needs, evaluate alternatives, develop practical technical solutions, and implement measurable improvements. 6. Develop and deliver technical workshops, training, and demonstrations for industry partners and workforce development programs. 7. Prepare technical reports, implementation summaries, proposals, presentations, and other communications for sponsors, customers, and stakeholders. 8. Support CAVS Extension laboratory and demonstration activities, including hands-on prototyping, pilot demonstrations, experiment planning, and student or intern engagement where applicable. 9. Maintain awareness of current and emerging methods in mechanical engineering, advanced manufacturing, automation, and smart manufacturing applications. 10. Build and maintain relationships with private industry, state and federal agencies, university partners, and other stakeholders. 11. Participate in grant proposal activities, and technology-transfer initiatives as needed. 12. Perform other duties as assigned under the general direction of CAVS Extension leadership. Minimum Qualifications: Research Engineer I – B.S. in Engineering Research Engineer II – B.S. in Engineering with at least two years of professional experience in a related area; Requires two years at previous level or equivalent Research Engineer III - B.S. in engineering; Four years of professional experience in a related area; requires two years at previous level or equivalent. Senior Research Engineer - B.S. in engineering; Six or more years of professional experience in a related area; requires two years at previous level or equivalent. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Comfortable working in industrial environments and engaging with clients • Strong problem-solving and troubleshooting skills • Strong written and oral communication skills • Strong analytical and technical skills with attention for detail and accuracy • Strong organizational skills and the ability to self-direct efforts to complete planning and documentation requirements • Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines • Self-motivated and collaborative, with a commitment to continuous learning and continuous improvement • Ability to work both independently and in a team-oriented, collaborative environment Working Conditions and Physical Effort • Frequent external imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one's control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days • Meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position; may involve conflict-resolution. • Work may involve exposure to industrial environments, including noise, machinery, and occasional lifting of equipment up to 40 pounds. • Travel to client sites is required; may include overnight travel, as needed. • Job frequently requires walking, standing, reaching, and handli Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online at www.jobs.msstate.edu by submitting a cover letter, resume, two letters of recommendation, and copy of your current transcripts. Any social security numbers included on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 944c13ef Last Name (required) 841b3736 Email (required) cb891a5f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 48806899 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Madison County, Mississippi, United States Madison County, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 9fd67a6c Last Name (required) 1f26b43f Email (required) 226ba148 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
