      "title": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor 511257 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 038600 - Psychology Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychology, full-time, 9-month, tenure track, beginning August 16, 2027. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Psychology is within the College of Arts & Sciences. It houses 24 full time faculty members, 800 undergraduates, and about 40 doctoral students in our Cognitive Science and Clinical Psychology Ph.D. programs. Area of Specialization: Clinical Psychology or Closely Related Field Anticipated Appointment Date: August 16, 2026 Tenure Track Status: Tenure-Track Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The new faculty member will teach undergraduate and graduate courses, including courses in the specialty area of clinical psychology. The successful applicants will maintain a program of scholarly research, apply for external funding, teach undergraduates and graduate courses, and supervise graduate students. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have completed a doctoral degree from an APA, CPA, or PCSAS accredited program by the time of appointment and be eligible for eventual licensure in Mississippi. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Work takes place in an office environment. Instructions for Applying: Interested applicants must apply online at https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter; curriculum vitae; statements on research and teaching; up to three pre/reprints; and contact information for at least three professional references. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Ty Stafford tws37@msstate.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 590079b5 Last Name (required) 2110c27f Email (required) bd3722eb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 65b3390c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 0bf99850 Last Name (required) 94a5b711 Email (required) 81772ca2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
