    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/sr-accounts-receivable-specialist-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-b6b52a22-1642-45f9-803d-72e4c7cb6eb7": {
      "title": "Sr. Accounts Receivable Specialist - Main Campus",
      "description": "Sr. Accounts Receivable Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Sr. Accounts Receivable Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Sr. Accounts Receivable Specialist 511283 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 450200 - Office of the Controller/Treasurer Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 22 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Under the direction of a team lead, this position is responsible for processing cashiering transactions, reconciling daily financial activity, and providing excellent customer service and operational support to students, parents, and departmental partners throughout the university. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Account Services serves as MSU's go-to resource for understanding costs, managing bills, making payments, and receiving refunds — all with professional, courteous support and a commitment to keeping things simple and transparent. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Assist customers in-person and on the phone with account concerns and payment related questions while adhering to FERPA regulations. 2. Process payments in the cashiering system and assist students and parents in interpreting their account balance. 3. Process cash receipt vouchers to record cash, check, and wire payments to various general ledger accounts. 4. Record departmental deposit bank receipts to the appropriate general ledger account. 5. Balance daily work and perform end-of-day reconciliation. 6. Maintain payroll paper check log and distribute payroll checks upon confirmation of direct deposit enrollment through Treasury Service 7. Assist in the implementation of new operational procedures. 8. Assists in the research and resolution of problems or questions related to departmental transactions as needed. 9. Verifies that cashiering operations documents are imaged properly and that the retention of the operation’s electronic or physical documents and data are held to departmental guidelines. 10. Maintains compliance with departmental security procedures, audit procedures and University business policies and procedures. Supervisory Responsibility: This position may supervise other non-exempt positions. Minimum Qualifications: Education High school diploma Experience (yrs.) 3-5 years plus the education listed above Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Well-developed interpersonal, teamwork, verbal and written communication skills • Demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing diversity • Demonstrated ability to manage/coordinate multiple tasks • Independent self-starter with strong work ethic • Strong customer service skills Working Conditions and Physical Effort • No unusual physical requirements. Requires limited lifting of files and records and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. • Frequent- External imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position; involves conflict-resolution or similar interactions involving emotional issues or stress on a regular basis. • Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 94feaf72 Last Name (required) c36f4808 Email (required) 88ca25e8 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 27de22bb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 6a588357 Last Name (required) 7fe175b9 Email (required) 42e1beb3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
