    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/asst-dir-business-operations-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Asst Dir, Business Operations - Main Campus",
      "description": "Asst Dir, Business Operations - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Asst Dir, Business Operations - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Asst Dir, Business Operations 511268 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 520193 - Student Housing - Administration Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 17 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Reporting to the Director for Business Operations and Guest Services for Housing & Residence Life, the Assistant Director is responsible for the management, supervision, and coordination of the business operations of the department, including purchasing/procurement, warehousing, inventory, student billing, reporting and database administration. Salary Grade : 16 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Provide direction, management, and oversight of purchasing/procurement, warehousing, inventory, student billing, reporting and database administration. 2. Implement strong processes, procedures, and internal controls for all business functions, particularly the purchasing function. Oversee to ensure adherence. 3. Supervise & direct personnel, including work allocation, training, and problem resolution; evaluate performance and make recommendations for personnel actions; motivate employees to achieve peak productivity and performance. 4. Communicate regularly with the Director for Business Operations and Guest Services; prepare reports, special analyses, and information reports; present recommendations for changes and/or improvements. 5. Develop long and short-range plans, direct staff, promote consistent standards, and ensure applicable procedures are followed in all business functions. 6. Implement financial controls and ensures adherence for all business functions; ensure compliance with university policies and procedures, state, and federal regulations. 7. Audit & analyze financial reports for accuracy and conformance to university and departmental policies and procedures. 8. Coordinate and process personnel actions, as appropriate. 9. Develop and implement systems to maintain records on inventories and compliance activities. 10. Evaluate and/or negotiate contracts for the purchase of services in coordination with the university purchasing department. 11. Serves as Database Administrator for the work order/asset/inventory computer system. 12. Perform related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration, Accounting, Finance or other appropriate discipline Experience (yrs.): 3 years directly related to university or general fund accounting and/or purchase function with strong management and communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: 5 years work experience in a university setting with strong background in managing accounting and/or business operations & purchasing functions. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Skill in organizing resources and establishing priorities. 2. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. 3. Ability to analyze and solve problems. 4. Strong interpersonal and communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies in a diverse community. 5. Knowledge of accounting procedures involving procurement, University and state rules and regulations. 6. Skill using AiM/AssetWorks work order management system. 7. Knowledge of inventory systems. 8. Knowledge and understanding of business management principles and practices. 9. Skill using BANNER system. 10. Ability to develop and maintain record-keeping systems and procedures. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. No unusual physical requirements. 2. Requires no heavy lifting, and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. 3. Frequent – Externally imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; irregular hours often anticipated; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position 4. Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. 5. Job requires standing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 10 pounds. 6. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Applicants must apply online and attach a cover letter and resume. Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 114a0454 Last Name (required) e7cd45d7 Email (required) 9c16c7c9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 21889782 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) a7a1743b Last Name (required) e3b19e73 Email (required) d59d3793 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Can