    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/instructor-i-ii-or-iii-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-98228e8d-a74c-4619-80fc-8085a9612f25": {
      "title": "Instructor I, II, or III - Main Campus",
      "description": "Instructor I, II, or III - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Instructor I, II, or III - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Instructor I, II, or III 511191 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 062900 - Computer Science and Engineering Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Sep 10 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Instructor in Computer Science and Engineering is under the administrative supervision of the Computer Science and Engineering Department Head. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate, and possibly split-level courses, as well as advising undergraduate students. Instructor will also serve on Undergraduate Studies Committee and aid in Undergraduate Curriculum development. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Computer Science and Engineering (http://www.cse.msstate.edu), part of the Bagley College of Engineering, at Mississippi State University is a vibrant and growing academic unit with a strong focus on education, research, and service. Mississippi State University is designated as both an R1 – Very High Research Activity Doctoral University under the Carnegie Classification and as a National Center of Academic Excellence in Cyber Operations, Cyber Defense Research, and Cyber Defense Education by the National Security Agency. The Department of Computer Science and Engineering is home to 28 faculty members and serves approximately 1,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The department offers undergraduate degrees in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Cybersecurity, and Artificial Intelligence, and jointly administers a Computer Engineering program with the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering. The Computer Science program includes concentrations in Artificial Intelligence, Systems, Human and Visual Computing, Computational Science, and General Computer Science. In addition, the department offers a Bachelor of Applied Science (B.A.S.) in Cybersecurity and three undergraduate minors: Computer Science, Software Engineering, and Artificial Intelligence. An accelerated B.S./M.S. program allows students to complete a Bachelor of Science in Computer Science or Software Engineering alongside a Master of Science in Computer Science in four academic years plus one calendar year. At the graduate level, the department offers M.S. and Ph.D. degrees in Computer Science, as well as standalone M.S. degrees in Cyber Security and Operations, Artificial Intelligence, and Data Science. Faculty also supervise graduate students in Computational Engineering. Certificate programs are available in Information Assurance, Cyber Operations, and Computational Biology. In the most recent fiscal year, the department reported research expenditures exceeding $4.6 million. Core research areas include cybersecurity, artificial intelligence, computational science, visualization and graphics, bioinformatics, parallel and distributed computing, software engineering, human-robot interaction, augmented and virtual reality, and computer science education. Faculty members are actively involved in several major university research centers, including the Center for Advanced Vehicular Systems, the Center for Cyber Innovation, the Center for Computational Science, and the Institute for Genomics, Biocomputing & Biotechnology. Anticipated Appointment Date: January 1, 2027 Tenure Track Status: Non-Tenure Track Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and possibly split-level courses Advise undergraduate students. Serve on Undergraduate Studies Committee. Aid in Undergraduate Curriculum development. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree in Computer Science or closely related field, or the equivalent in training and experience. Preferred Qualifications: PhD in Computer Science or closely related field, or the equivalent in training and experience. Teaching experience in Computer Science or closely related field at the college level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: See minimum and preferred qualifications. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Typical office/lab environment. Instructions for Applying: Interested candidates must apply at www.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach cover letter, curriculum vitae, names and contact information for at least three professional references, and a statement (limited to three pages) that describes research and educational interests. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 35a24d8b Last Name (required) 93a1ead7 Email (required) ed7c587d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 0f047b25 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 1e6cc2e6 Last Name (required) 19f2b288 Email (required) aeb70995 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
