    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-l-p-s-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-96a36763-70d9-4aae-ac6f-74a17732a734": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) 511152 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 031900 - Chemistry Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The successful candidate will play a leading role in developing innovative optical spectroscopic instrumentation and measurement methodologies, including unpolarized, linearly polarized, and circularly polarized transmission, scattering, photoluminescence, and emerging multimodal spectroscopic platforms. Working closely with faculty collaborators and an interdisciplinary team of postdoctoral associates, graduate students, and undergraduate researchers, the candidate will contribute to cutting-edge research while developing expertise in proposal preparation, project leadership, mentoring, and technology commercialization. The position is particularly suited for candidates pursuing careers in academia, national laboratories, or advanced industrial research. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. Department Profile: For information on the Department of Chemistry, please visit www.chemistry.msstate.edu Area of Specialization: Chemistry Anticipated Appointment Date: Fall 2026 Tenure Track Status: n/A Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate is expected to become a scientific leader within the research group and will have opportunities to: · Conduct innovative research in optical spectroscopy, scientific instrumentation, and quantitative measurement science. · Publish high-impact research in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at national and international conferences. · Contribute intellectually to the development of new research directions and interdisciplinary collaborations. · Participate in the preparation of competitive research proposals to federal funding agencies and contribute to long-term strategic research planning. · Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and intellectually stimulating research environment. · Contribute to establishing the laboratory as a national leader in next-generation optical measurement science. Minimum Qualifications: · A Ph.D. in Chemistry, Physics, Optical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Materials Science, or a closely related discipline (completed before the appointment begins). · Demonstrated research accomplishments in optical spectroscopy, scientific instrumentation, physical chemistry, optical physics, or related fields, as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications. · Strong experimental, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to conduct independent research. · Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: · Quantitative optical measurements involving biological, chemical, or nanomaterial systems · Scientific instrument design, automation, and optical system integration · Computer Programming (Python, LabVIEW,or related languages) · Student mentoring or interdisciplinary collaborative research Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting and bending. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt chemicals, etc. Instructions for Applying: 1. Cover Letter describing research interests, qualifications, career goals, and including the names and contact information for three professional references. 2. Curriculum Vitae including a complete list of publications and links to representative publications, when available. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 93f2bc3f Last Name (required) f5e43ad7 Email (required) ca622c20 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 900fa9a4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) af752bc2 Last Name (required) c8b7acc8 Email (required) 61673b23 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-l-p-s-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-ccbc318d-5ff4-471a-a479-a7b7309fa171": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) 511153 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 031900 - Chemistry Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Postdoctoral Associate will conduct advanced research bridging electronic structure theory and data-driven methods, leveraging both theoretical frameworks and machine learning (ML) models to predict the behavior of quantum materials. The successful candidate will play a key role in developing innovative computational approaches and scientific software. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: For information on the Department of Chemistry, please visit www.chemistry.msstate.edu Area of Specialization: Chemistry Anticipated Appointment Date: Fall 2026 Tenure Track Status: n/A Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Design and implement machine learning models to accelerate quantum chemistry calculations, enabling rapid, data-driven materials discovery and force field development. · Lead the dissemination of research findings through peer-reviewed journal publications, manuscript preparation, and presentations at regional and national academic conferences. · Contribute to ongoing development, optimization, and maintenance of custom computational software packages. · Assist in preliminary data generation for extramural grant proposals. Minimum Qualifications: · PhD in Chemistry, Physics, Materials Science, or closely related disciplines. · Strong background in theoretical chemistry with demonstrated experience performing electronic structure calculations. · Proficiency in writing and maintaining scientific computational software. Preferred Qualifications: · Hands-on experience training, developing, and deploying machine learning models for chemical or physical applications. · Familiarity with strongly correlated electronic structure methodologies and implementing these methods in computational software. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting and bending. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. Instructions for Applying: Interested candidates must apply to msujobs.msstate.edu and submit the following materials: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae (CV), including a full list of publications. 3. Three most relevant publications. 4. A one-page statement of research interests. 5. Contact information for three references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f384bf4d Last Name (required) 5a692c70 Email (required) a48ab4af Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 71a8e219 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 8beca681 Last Name (required) 4d3371f5 Email (required) 8039e06d Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/research-associate-copiah-county-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate - Copiah County, Mississippi, United States Research Associate - Copiah County, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Associate 511245 Copiah County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 013500 - Truck Crops Branch Exp Station Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: To assist with the research work involved in establishing, maintaining, and conducting horticulture studies, collecting and analyzing data, and processing samples from experiments. The individual will be part of a research team for a horticulture research station. The person will be expected to work independently and in cooperation with faculty, staff, and field labor. The applicant is also expected to perform work assignments outlined by the research professor. Salary Grade : 13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Central Mississippi Research and Extension Center (CMREC) is one of four Research and Extension Centers in the MSU System and located in Raymond, MS. The Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station (MAFES) - Truck Crops Branch Experiment Station is administratively associated with the CMREC and located in Crystal Springs, MS. The station's primary mission is to conduct research to benefit the Mississippi vegetable, ornamental, fruit, and/or nut industries. Anticipated Appointment Date: November 1, 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: These duties include: 1. Following research protocols, planning and implementing field experiments, and harvesting/recording data in the field, greenhouse, and lab setting data 2. Planting, fertilizing, scouting for plant problems, cross-pollinating, propagating with cuttings and tissue culture, spraying, weeding, weighing, counting, cataloging, measuring, and harvesting 3. Growing and maintaining quality plant material in the field, greenhouse, and lab setting 4. Greenhouse production, including scheduling, monitoring the control system, and checking pH and EC levels etc. 5. Safely handling, mixing, and applying pesticides and fertilizers 6. Meticulous record keeping 7. Data recording and entry into computer spreadsheets 8. Data analysis and technical writing 9. Assisting with field days, sales, and other activities on the experiment station as needed 10. Updating the trial garden website 11. Perform other duties as assigned by the supervisor Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor of Science Degree Rank and salary will be commensurate with education and/or experience. Preferred Qualifications: Master's Degree in Horticulture or related field with a minimum of 3 years experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Time management and organization skills required Knowledge of data analysis and experimental design preferred Fundamental knowledge of plant biology and genetics preferred Proficiency with computer programs, specifically Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, and PowerPoint), and initiative to learn new computer programs as needed Ability to conduct experiments within a laboratory, including proper pipette use and ability to follow written protocols preferred Ability to maintain lab sanitation by practicing proper disinfection and disposal procedures for tissue and cultural waste Working Conditions and Physical Effort Willingness and ability to work in an outdoor garden environment are essential. Considerable physical activity. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing, or pulling required of objects up to and often over 50 pounds. Physical work is a large portion of the job. Work may involve moderate exposure to unusual elements such as extreme temperatures, dirt, dust, fumes, smoke, unpleasant odors, and/or loud noises. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online at msujobs.msstate.edu. Letters of recommendation are strongly encouraged. A cover letter, resume, and educational transcripts will be required. When submitting documents and transcripts, applicants should redact (mark out) their Social Security Number (SSN) anywhere it appears before creating the PDF and uploading it. Do not mark or alter your transcript other than redacting the SSN. Please contact Dr. Shaun Broderick at (601) 647-1341 for additional information. Screening Date: September 29, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) e0ee207c Last Name (required) 9de39755 Email (required) 1b789d66 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done 