    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/coordinator-school-of-nursing-enrollment-services-meridian-campus-meridian-ms-mississippi-united-states-riley-campus-meridian-ms-riley-center-meridian-ms": {
      "title": "Coordinator, School of Nursing Enrollment Services - Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Center",
      "description": "Coordinator, School of Nursing Enrollment Services - Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Coordinator, School of Nursing Enrollment Services - Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Coordinator, School of Nursing Enrollment Services 511264 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313218 - Meridian - School of Nursing Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 14 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Nursing Student Enrollment Director serves as the primary coordinator for student recruitment, admissions, enrollment, and student-facing communications within the School of Nursing. The position is responsible for developing and maintaining prospective student pipelines, supporting applicants through the admissions process, coordinating recruitment and outreach activities, managing admissions and enrollment workflows, and collaborating with faculty and staff to support student matriculation and success. This position serves as a key point of contact for prospective students and applicants and helps ensure a seamless experience from initial inquiry through enrollment. The role works closely with university partners, faculty, staff, and external stakeholders to advance enrollment goals and support the continued growth of the School of Nursing. Salary Grade : 14 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The following examples are intended as illustrations only of the various types of duties assigned to this position. The absence of specific statements of duties does not exclude those tasks from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment of the position. Recruitment and Outreach Develop and implement recruitment strategies to support enrollment goals across School of Nursing academic programs. Represent the School of Nursing at recruitment events, college fairs, information sessions, community events, professional meetings, and other outreach activities. Cultivate and maintain relationships with prospective students, community colleges, universities, healthcare organizations, and other recruitment partners. Coordinate and facilitate on-campus and virtual recruitment events, information sessions, open houses, and student engagement activities. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and university partners to identify and develop recruitment pipelines that support enrollment growth. Assist with development and dissemination of promotional materials, recruitment communications, and program information. Admissions and Enrollment Management Serve as a primary point of contact for prospective students regarding admission requirements, application procedures, program options, and enrollment processes. Coordinate admissions-related activities and workflows, including application review processes, applicant communications, and admissions tracking. Manage and maintain NursingCAS and other admissions-related systems and processes as assigned. Monitor applicant progress through the admissions funnel and conduct timely follow-up to support application completion and enrollment. Collaborate with university offices to ensure efficient processing of admissions, registration, financial aid, and enrollment-related matters. Provide unofficial transcript reviews and general guidance regarding prerequisite and admission requirements as appropriate. Student Communication and Program Navigation Maintain regular communication with prospective students, applicants, admitted students, and other stakeholders throughout the recruitment and enrollment process. Assist students in understanding program pathways, admission requirements, timelines, and available resources. Serve as a liaison connecting prospective and newly admitted students with faculty, advisors, and program leadership as appropriate. Support new student onboarding, orientation, and transition-to-enrollment activities. Coordinate communications designed to improve student engagement, enrollment yield, and retention. Data Management and Enrollment Analytics Develop and maintain databases and systems that track prospective students, applicants, admissions outcomes, enrollment activity, and recruitment efforts. Monitor recruitment, admissions, and enrollment metrics and prepare reports as requested. Maintain accurate records of recruitment contacts, communications, applications, admissions decisions, and enrollment outcomes. Utilize data to support continuous improvement of recruitment and enrollment processes. Collaboration and Program Support Work collaboratively with program directors, faculty, university enrollment personnel, marketing staff, and other stakeholders to support School of Nursing enrollment goals. Assist in developing communication plans, publications, and outreach initiatives that support program visibility and student recruitment. Participate in strategic planning and implementation activities related to recruitment, admissions, enrollment, and student success. Support special projects and initiatives that advance the mission and growth of the School of Nursing. Perform other duties as assigned. DECISION MAKING / GUIDELINES This role requires limited decision making and fiscal responsibilities. SUPERVISORY AUTHORITY This role does not require supervision. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Experience: Two years of experience in recruitment, admissions, enrollment management, student services, marketing, communications, customer service, higher education administration, healthcare administration, or a related field. Substitutions Allowed: N/A Required License / Certification: N/A Preferred Qualifications: Experience working in higher education recruitment, admissions, enrollment management, or student services. Experience with graduate admissions processes. Experience using CRM, enrollment management, or applicant tracking systems. Experience with NursingCAS or similar centralized application systems. Experience developing and implementing recruitment and communication plans. Experience working with nursing, healthcare, or professional academic programs. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to build relationships with prospective students, faculty, staff, and external partners. Strong organizational and project management skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to analyze and utilize enrollment and recruitment data to support decision-making. Knowledge of customer relationship management and student engagement principles. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and database systems. Ability to exercise sound judgment and maintain confidentiality. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. No or very limited exposure to physical risk. No or very limited physical effort required. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply only at www.msujobs.msstate.edu by submitting a cover letter, resume, and the contact information for three professional references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 5e12c695 Last Name (required) f57f5c43 Email (required) e87c6595 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 97a39bcd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 49b57747 Last Name (required) 1da0a7c8 Email (required) 07b859b0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
