    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-l-p-s-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-e9bf0870-bcae-4aa1-8302-2646369dc16b": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) 511209 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 031900 - Chemistry Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 10 2026 Position Function: Vacancy for a postdoctoral associate focused on the synthesis of organic fluorophores and cellular culturing Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: For more information on the Department of Chemistry, please visit www.chemistry.msstate.edu Essential Duties and Responsibilities: · Design and synthesize functional organic fluorophores and related molecular probes. · Develop and optimize synthetic methodologies for dye functionalization. · Culture and maintain mammalian cell lines under sterile conditions. · Evaluate dye uptake, localization, cytotoxicity, and imaging performance in cultured cells. · Perform fluorescence microscopy, confocal microscopy, flow cytometry, and related cellular imaging techniques. · Analyze experimental data and correlate molecular structure with biological performance. · Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers in both synthetic chemistry and cell biology. · Prepare manuscripts, present research findings at scientific conferences, and assist with proposal development. Minimum Qualifications: · A Ph.D. in Organic Chemistry, Chemical Biology, Medicinal Chemistry, Biochemistry, or a closely related field. · Demonstrated expertise in multistep organic synthesis and compound characterization (NMR, MS, chromatography, etc.). · Experience with mammalian cell culture and sterile laboratory techniques. · Excellent written and oral communication skills · Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within a multidisciplinary research team. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to candidates with experience in one or more of the following: · Fluorescent probe or dye synthesis. · Confocal or fluorescence microscopy. · Flow cytometry. · Cell viability and cytotoxicity assays. · Image analysis software (ImageJ/Fiji or equivalent). · Experience with NIR/SWIR imaging, molecular imaging, or chemical biology. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting and bending. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. Instructions for Applying: Applicants should submit: 1. A cover letter describing research interests and relevant experience. 2. A current curriculum vitae. 3. A one-page summary of previous research accomplishments. 4. Contact information for three professional references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 65c9fb25 Last Name (required) cdc6d913 Email (required) 6b25bcbd Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 617522f0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Ti