    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/program-assistant-various-locations-in-mississippi-mississippi-united-states-8869cd10-9320-4272-928c-b6ef8ea08738": {
      "title": "Program Assistant",
      "description": "Program Assistant - Various locations in Mississippi, Mississippi, United States Program Assistant - Various locations in Mississippi, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Program Assistant 511208 Various locations in Mississippi Mississippi - Not located on main campus 050405 - CEP-Migrant Ed Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 3 2026 Position Function: The Mississippi Migrant Education Program is a federally funded program geared towards providing migrant students with supplemental education to bridge learning gaps due to the migratory lifestyle. Applicants should be highly self-motivated to provide education services to underserved students in rural areas across the state of Mississippi. The function of the Program Assistant is to support the Migrant Education Program (MEP) through advocacy, outreach, family engagement, and recruitment assistance activities. This position assists migrant children, youth, and families in accessing educational and community resources while promoting awareness of services available through the Migrant Education Program. The Program Assistant assists with identification of potential migrant families and serves as a liaison between migrant families, schools, community organizations, and program staff to help address barriers to educational success. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : 9 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: As a land-grant university, MSU is proud to house the Mississippi Migrant Education Service Center which serves agricultural families throughout the state. The Mississippi Migrant Education Service Center is a federal program that offers supplemental and supportive educational services to ensure that migrant children have access to all opportunities that a public education offers. The Mississippi Migrant Education Service Center is funded through the Mississippi Department of Education and is housed at Mississippi State University. Area of Specialization: CEP-Migrant Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Assist with outreach efforts to identify and connect migrant children, youth, and families with available educational services and resources. · Attend state or local and on-going training and meetings including professional development and recruitment support to fulfill the Title I, Part C Migrant Education Program responsibilities. · Support recruitment activities by helping locate prospective migrant families and referring potential participants to program recruiters for eligibility determination. · Establish and maintain positive relationships with migrant families, school personnel, community agencies, agricultural employers, and other stakeholders. · Serve as a liaison between migrant families and schools to facilitate communication and encourage student and family engagement. · Fully understand and establish proper eligibility determinations based on the guidelines outlined in the recruiter’s manual, the Non-Regulatory Guidance, and the statutes governing the MEP. · Follow proper procedures and protocol regarding all identification and recruitment activities. · Provide advocacy and support services to migrant students and families by identifying needs and connecting them with appropriate educational, health, and community resources. · Assist families with understanding school procedures, available services, and educational opportunities. · Participate in community events, school activities, and outreach initiatives designed to increase awareness of the Migrant Education Program. · Maintain records of outreach, advocacy, and family engagement activities as required by program guidelines. · Collaborate with program staff to support student success initiatives and special projects. · Assist with parent engagement activities, workshops, and meetings, including support for Parent Advisory Council activities when appropriate. · Travel extensively (may include weekends) throughout assigned service areas to conduct outreach and provide services to migrant families. · Perform other duties as assigned in support of program goals and objectives. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High school diploma or equivalent. 2. Bilingual (English/Spanish) proficiency 3. Valid driver's license and reliable transportation. 4. Ability to communicate effectively with students, families, school personnel, and community partners. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Experience working with children, youth, families, or community-based programs. 2. Experience working with migrant, multilingual, or underserved populations. 3. Knowledge of community resources and support services available to families. 4. Strong interpersonal, organizational, and communication skills. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Speaks Spanish fluently. Knowledge of state agencies and community services organizations that serve migratory families. Ability to travel extensively. Working Conditions and Physical Effort This position requires travel throughout assigned service areas, including visits to schools, community agencies, homes, and agricultural work sites. Evening and weekend work may be required to accommodate family schedules and community events. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Complete the online application and include resume, a cover letter, and minimum of 3 references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 8e766f07 Last Name (required) ddee770b Email (required) 3d352551 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert f53d3059 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Various locations in Mississippi, Mississippi, United States Various locations in Mississippi, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 3436218e Last Name (required) e3c42f57 Email (required) 4a57697b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
