    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/planning-and-assessment-coordinator-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Planning and Assessment Coordinator - Main Campus",
      "description": "Planning and Assessment Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Planning and Assessment Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Planning and Assessment Coordinator 511205 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 441106 - Student Affairs Assessment Office Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 31 2026 Position Function: The Planning and Assessment Coordinator is primarily responsible for facilitating programs, services, and activities in support of the Division of Student Affairs’ goals, objectives, and strategies. Working in the Office of Planning and Assessment, activities include, but are not limited to, assisting departments in the development of success strategies, coordinating activities across the division in support of strategic goals and objectives, and working with the Vice President for Student Affairs team in the development and implementation of policies and procedures. Salary Grade : 13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The following examples are intended as illustrations only of the various types of duties assigned in positions allocated to this classification. The absence of specific statements of duties does not exclude those tasks from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment of the position. 1. Working with student affairs teams, committees, and leadership, coordinate, facilitate, and manage special events in support of student affairs including professional development programming and training, new employee orientation, and student success initiatives. 2. Coordinate special projects and activities designed to reinforce plans, policies, and procedures. 3. Review current division-wide strategies, goals, and policies, and conduct analysis to determine if updates or changes need to be made; make recommendations to student affairs professionals and leadership in the development of new strategies, goals, and policies. 4. Look for, recommend, and facilitate effective collaborative opportunities that can achieve common goals and objectives. 5. Assist with the strategic planning process at the division and department level. 6. Work with departments to determine assessment and planning needs and conduct other research activities. 7. Facilitate relationships between departments and other campus partners, including but not limited to the Office of Institutional Research and Effectiveness. 8. Assume other duties as assigned by the Assistant Director, Office of Planning and Assessment and the Office of VP for Student Affairs. Minimum Qualifications: Master's Degree in Higher Education, Student Affairs / College Student Personnel, Public Administration, or other related field and one year of relevant experience in a student affairs setting. Preferred Qualifications: • Understanding of Student Learning and processes. • Ability to conduct data analysis. • Superior leadership and management skills (including interpersonal and organizational). • Excellent presentation skills. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Knowledge of and experience with Microsoft Office Suite of programs. 2. Ability to work effectively with other staff members. 3. Strong interpersonal skills, including strong oral, written, and listening communication capabilities. 4. Ability to research and understand higher education models, especially those applicable to Student Learning, Assessment, and Strategic Planning. Working Conditions and Physical Effort • No unusual physical requirements. Requires limited lifting of files and records and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. • Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. • Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 28f22bbe Last Name (required) c24dbb5b Email (required) cdee5f4f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 1bb8aa24 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 13a45335 Last Name (required) fe4252e1 Email (required) 40767fd7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
