    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-teaching-professor-meridian-campus-meridian-ms-mississippi-united-states-riley-campus-meridian-ms-riley-center-meridian-ms-993db161-2e4a-4944-911d-f202d8084b07": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor - Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Center",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor - Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor - Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States - Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor 511168 Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313203 - Meridian Healthcare Administration Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Position Function: The Mississippi State University Meridian Campus is seeking an Assistant or Associate Teaching Professor for the Department of Healthcare Administration. This is a 9-month teaching track [non-tenure earning] faculty position. This faculty position will represent the Healthcare Administration Program on the Mississippi State University Starkville campus. The Department of Healthcare Administration is housed within the School of Health Professions on the MSU-Meridian campus. The successful candidate is expected to travel regularly to the Meridian campus to participate in department meetings, school meetings, faculty activities, and other programmatic and institutional responsibilities as appropriate. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Please visit our website at https://www.bas.msstate.edu/programs/healthcare-administration for information regarding Healthcare Administration. Area of Specialization: Healthcare Administration Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Teach in-person courses on the Starkville campus in Healthcare Administration areas such as Managed Care, U.S. Healthcare Systems, Ethical Issues, Law and Regulation, Healthcare Policy, and Healthcare Marketing. Teach online courses as applicable. Courses will be assigned based on programmatic needs. 2. Support program marketing and student recruitment initiatives by participating in recruitment events, community outreach activities, open houses, information sessions, and tabling events to enhance program visibility and enrollment. 3. Engage with prospective students, community partners, and other stakeholders to promote the Healthcare Administration program and contribute to student recruitment and retention efforts. 4. Mentor students and contribute to their academic, professional, and career development. 5. Provide service to the department, school, and university through committee work, accreditation efforts, community engagement, and other institutional initiatives. Minimum Qualifications: 1. Earned doctorate from a regionally accredited university in Healthcare Management, Healthcare Administration, or a closely related field. ABD status applicants will be considered if expected completion date is before appointment. 2. Record of teaching and service at the university level. 3. Demonstrated experience in program marketing, student recruitment, enrollment growth, community outreach, and stakeholder engagement in higher education. 4. Proven ability to promote academic programs through recruitment events, open houses, high school and community college visits, tabling events, and other outreach activities that enhance program visibility and student enrollment. 5. Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues in the department and across disciplines. Rank and salary are commensurate with education and experience. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Established record of teaching applicable to Healthcare Administration for appointment at the appropriate rank. 2. Ability to build partnerships with healthcare organizations, community stakeholders, and educational institutions to support program growth, experiential learning opportunities, and workforce development. 3. Demonstrated experience with on-campus and online instruction, development, and delivery. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Higher Education Experience Professional Education Experience Working Conditions and Physical Effort Office Setting Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu by submitting a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and the contact information for three professional references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 516cc3c0 Last Name (required) f5b3195f Email (required) 48eccdb6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 47cf95d6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Meridian Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) c8f513fb Last Name (required) d02d3598 E