      "title": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor 510841 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 041300 - Management & Information Systems Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Jul 16 2026 Position Function: A full-time tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level to teach courses in Strategy for Fall 2027 at the undergraduate and graduate level for the Management & Information Systems Department. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Management and Information Systems Department Area of Specialization: Strategy Anticipated Appointment Date: August 16, 2027 Tenure Track Status: Tenure-Track Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses. Engage in research that leads to publications in top journals. Fulfill service obligations to department, college, and university. Minimum Qualifications: Successful candidate must have a Ph.D. in Management or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to teach Strategy. Demonstrated ability to do research that leads to publications in top management journals, especially family business research. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to conduct quality teaching. Ability to conduct research that leads to publications in top journals. Willingness and ability to provide appropriate level of department, college, and university service. Effective written and oral communication skills. Ability to work with students and colleagues. Working Conditions and Physical Effort No unusual physical requirements. Requires no heavy lifting, and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. Instructions for Applying: Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Submit cover letter and current vita. Two letters of recommendation should either be attached to application or emailed directly from writer to Jennifer Sexton (jsexton@business.msstate.edu). Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 12b6730f Last Name (required) 474abfcc Email (required) 15bb8b0f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 8fb1e5d6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) a6ea4a71 Last Name (required) 313598d7 Email (required) b299179b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
