    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/social-media-specialist-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-60647848-6c2f-413b-a6cd-4e0817e9994c": {
      "title": "Social Media Specialist - Main Campus",
      "description": "Social Media Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Social Media Specialist - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Social Media Specialist 510958 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 017600 - MAFES Administrative Overhead Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Jul 20 2026 Position Function: Develop and maintain a social media strategy for multiple accounts within the College of Forest Resources, College of Agriculture and Life Sciences, Forest and Wildlife Research Center and the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station. Produce content (including stories, photography, graphics and videos) for all platforms with an emphasis on social media. Manage metrics. Serve as a resource for departmental training. Optimize day-to-day social media. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: See mafes.msstate.edu and fwrc.msstate.edu Anticipated Appointment Date: August 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Develop and maintain a comprehensive social media strategy to expand our reach and to establish social media as a sustainable communications channel for building our MSU brand. 2. Manage agriculture and natural resources marketing presence in social media networking sites, and work with the website development team to ensure social media tools are kept up to date. 3. Write clear, compelling communications and stories for publication on websites, email campaigns, newsletters and social media outlets to engage various audiences (prospective students, members of academia and government organizations, stakeholders, etc.). 4. Provide training as needed to departmental staff on best practices for creating, managing, monitoring and developing content for social media channels. 5. Establish and monitor benchmarks for measuring the impact of social media efforts, and report analytics on the effectiveness of such efforts. Benchmark against competitors and make recommendations for improvements. 6. Assist in integrating social media into overall marketing initiatives for Agriculture and Natural Resources Marketing. 7. Work with the Director of Agriculture and Natural Resources Marketing to gather and create branded content ensuring consistency across multiple marketing channels. 8. Work with the Director of Agriculture and Natural Resources Marketing to create and maintain content calendars for all departmental communication efforts. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High School Diploma. Experience: Four (4) years' experience similar to duties described. An equivalent combination of related education and related experience may be considered for this position. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in communications. Experience with online monitoring and measurement platforms is preferred, including but not limited to Facebook Insights, YouTube Insights, and Google Analytics. Strong computer skills, specifically in Adobe Creative Cloud. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Skill in organizing resources and establishing priorities. 2. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. 3. Ability to foster a cooperative work environment. 4. Ability to evaluate and edit the content, structure, and format of a range of written material. 5. Proven knowledge of and experience using appropriate technologies. Advanced computer skills and technical ability are expected. 6. Skills in the use of database management, word processing, spreadsheet, and/or presentation software. 7. Knowledge of communication principles, media, and public relations techniques. 8. Ability to plan, develop, and coordinate multiple projects and events. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. No unusual physical requirements. 2. Requires no heavy lifting, and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. 3. Frequent - Externally imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; irregular hours may be anticipated; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position. 4. Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands 5. Job requires standing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 10 pounds 6. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically 7. Hearing requirements: Heavy telephone contact requires ability to hear and respond to telephone conversations Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply at www.msujobs.msstate.edu Screening Date: July 27, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) d4e73123 Last Name (required) 1e6f5057 Email (required) 4626c7e0 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 961614d7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 2a445eaa Last Name (required) 50a3f5e9 Email (required) fdb1b3cd Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
