    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/program-coordinator-cals-mafes-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Program Coordinator, CALS-MAFES - Main Campus",
      "description": "Program Coordinator, CALS-MAFES - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Program Coordinator, CALS-MAFES - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Program Coordinator, CALS-MAFES 511139 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 010100 - MAFES Administration Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 20 2026 Position Function: Coordinates projects, processes, and activities and provides services for the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS) and the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station (MAFES). Serves as a central administrative staff member responsible for planning College and Experiment Station level events as well as scheduling for CALS and MAFES facilities. Salary Grade : Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: For more information on the Mississippi Agricultural and Forestry Experiment Station (MAFES), please visit www.mafes.msstate.edu For more information on the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences (CALS), please visit www.cals.msstate.edu Anticipated Appointment Date: September 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Plan, coordinate, and execute a diverse range of events for the CALS Dean and MAFES Director’s Office. 2. Manage event budgets, negotiate vendor contracts, and ensure cost-effective yet high-quality outcomes. 3. Oversee all event logistics, including venue selection, catering, AV/tech setup, décor, and on-site coordination. 4. Maintain detailed records of events, including setup requirements, attendance, and post-event feedback. 5. Evaluate event success through feedback surveys and post-event reports, using insights to improve future programming. 6. Manage and maintain the CALS Dean and MAFES Director’s Office facility scheduling and invoicing, ensuring accurate and up-to-date bookings for meeting rooms, event spaces, and specialized facilities. 7. Assist with student/visitor engagement and guest reception. 8. Supervise student workers. 9. Provides backup support for other administrative staff in CALS/MAFES. 10. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree Preferred Qualifications: • Experience with managing events, including planning and executing events. • Experience working with college students, their parents, or guardians, and with academic administrators and faculty Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Knowledge of word processing and spread sheet programs. 2. Excellent interpersonal, written and oral communication skills required. 3. Excellent organizational skills Working Conditions and Physical Effort • Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. • Some physical activity required for event setup. Requires lifting, pushing, or pulling of objects up to 50 pounds. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online at msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include cover letter, current resume, and copy of unofficial transcript(s) with all SSNs redacted. Screening Date: September 3, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 62b5a1a2 Last Name (required) d2c1633c Email (required) caf1d871 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert cb905d2b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) f96815ea Last Name (required) 0c8b8f29 Email (required) 4181aee9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
