    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/athletic-academic-counselor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-2d5a2b22-e8cc-411f-af1c-9c679bdf4391": {
      "title": "Athletic Academic Counselor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Athletic Academic Counselor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Athletic Academic Counselor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Athletic Academic Counselor 511022 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 300601 - The Dept of Ath Acad Supp Serv Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 19 2026 Position Function: Provides assistance to the Assistant Athletic Director for Academics in order to help facilitate the academic development and progress of student-athletes toward degree completion in assigned sport. This position reports to the Assistant Athletic Director for Academics. This position will provide academic assistance to student-athletes in one or more sports, assist with departmental record keeping activities, provide assistance with departmental liaison activities, and will supervise a minimum of one graduate assistant. Salary Grade : 15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure for salary ranges. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: A. Provides academic assistance to student-athletes: 1. Assists in enrollment procedures 2. Assists with admissions process 3. Provides student counseling, as requested 4. Assists with on-campus recruiting 5. Works with faculty and coaches, as needed, to monitor class attendance, study hall attendance, and reports on student progress, and performs other related tasks. B. Assists with departmental record keeping activities: 1. Assists with the maintenance of student-athlete records 2. Assists in the maintenance of current information on student-athletes' academic degree program 3. Assists in the maintenance of accurate records relative to student-athlete eligibility 4. Assists with reports and surveys related to academics C. Provides assistance with departmental liaison activities. 1. Provides liaison services with University faculty, as well as admissions and registrar personnel. 2. Assists with informing coaches on academic matters relative to Student-Athletes D. Performs related duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility Supervision of student-workers, tutors, and/ or interns as needed. The above essential duties are representative of major duties of positions in this position. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Other duties may be assigned to the above consistent with the knowledge, skills and abilities required for the job. Not all of the duties may be assigned to a position. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Education, Counseling, or related field with at least 2-4 years of experience in an Athletic Academic Office on a university campus. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree in Education, Counseling, or related field with at least 4-5 years of experience in an Athletic Academic Office on a university campus. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Must have strong interpersonal and organizational skills 2. Knowledge of Grades First 3. Knowledge of NCAA and SEC rules and regulations 4. Excellent verbal/written communication skills 5. Computer /Technological skills 6. Able to work with a diverse group of people with various backgrounds, education levels, and cultural differences Working Conditions and Physical Effort • Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. • No or very limited exposure to physical risk. • No or very limited physical effort required. • Concentrates on documents for periods of time up to two hours in length. • Types documents for periods of time up to an hour at a time without a break. • Ability to work at night, and on weekends. • Ability to meet deadlines, to work after hours, and to travel as needed on a limited basis. • Ability to sit at computer for extended periods of time. Instructions for Applying: All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu and include a cover letter, resume, and the complete contact information of 3 professional references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 92ca4362 Last Name (required) f0c2c30a Email (required) 21217924 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert eb2dabd1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) f16e36c4 Last Name (required) 0222abed Email (required) 0bba78a0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
