    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/agricultural-technician-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-87861af9-429e-4291-a523-83dec9cc41d2": {
      "title": "Agricultural Technician - Main Campus",
      "description": "Agricultural Technician - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Agricultural Technician - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Agricultural Technician 511142 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 080200 - Forest Operations Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 18 2026 Position Function: Responsible for upkeep of grounds and seasonal mowing for FWRC, which includes Forest Products Complex, Acorn Building, the Blackjack Facilities, and Dorman Lake. Will help with daily functions at the Forest Operations shop, that include but are not limited to motor pool repair, equipment operation and upkeep, light construction and building maintenance, as well as special projects assigned to Forest Operations by the Dean’s Office. This position will answer directly to the Grounds, Maintenance, and Equipment Coordinator of Forest Operations. Salary Grade : 10 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Anticipated Appointment Date: October 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Provide seasonal grass-cutting for FWRC facilities, will supervise student workers when appropriate. 2. Maintain the lawncare schedule of the included grounds in a timely manner, working with mowers, trimmers, edger, blower, and other lawncare equipment. 3. Operate farm equipment to remove trees, clip roadsides and ditches. 4. Responsible for upkeep and maintenance of all lawncare equipment. May source parts and supplies as needed. 5. May build sheds, lean-to’s, fences, decks or other structures. 6. Assist in implementing detailed landscape plans; assist in modifications and adjustments to landscape to comply with the needs of the FWRC and MSU regulations. 7. Assist Forest Operations in vehicle fleet management when necessary. 8. May use power and hand tools to assist with various tasks in carpentry, construction, mechanics and maintenance. 9. Maintain knowledge of all applicable equipment and machinery, including tractors, excavators, backhoes, etc. 10. Knowledge of lawncare practices, chemical applications, insect/disease control, plant nutrition, and pruning methods. 11. Able to adapt to changes, solve problems and prioritize. 12. Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High school diploma or GED Certifications and/or Licensures: Valid driver’s license Certifications and/or Licensures: 1. Valid driver’s license. 2. Must obtain a Certified Pesticide Applicators Certificate within 90 days of employment or complete the worker/handler training, whichever is applicable. Substitution allowed: An equivalent combination of related education and related experience may be considered for this position. Preferred Qualifications: Two years of related experience in lawncare. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Ability to work with others. 2. Ability to operate equipment. 3. Knowledge of agricultural operations. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting, bending or other physical exertion. Often exposed to extreme weather conditions such as heat, cold, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. Routing deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing, or pulling required of objects up to 25 pounds. Job occasionally requires climbing or balancing and lifting more than 100 pounds. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applications must be made online on the Mississippi State University Employment opportunities website via the link: www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include a resume with your application. Screening Date: August 25, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) cde2b556 Last Name (required) f7342fb7 Email (required) 9e089ce2 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 98c62db9 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) bef7581c Last Name (required) 28532406 Email (required) 917c58e1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
