    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/student-care-coordinator-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Care Coordinator - Main Campus",
      "description": "Student Care Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Student Care Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Care Coordinator 511130 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 410400 - Student Counseling Services Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 17 2026 Position Function: The Student Care Coordinator (SCC) reports to the Director of MSU Student Counseling Services and the Dean of Students serving in the Division of Student Affairs. The Student Care Coordinator (SCC) is responsible for helping students navigate care and concern challenges they face at MSU. The SCC works within the existing Care and Concern network of the DOS office and within the framework of the Student Counseling Center when doing clinical counseling and when performing outreach/educational programming. Additionally, the SCC is responsible for providing intervention and consultation services for students, faculty and staff as needed. The SCC is also a referral resource to faculty and staff in the various academic units and staff departments at MSU where they will serve as an embedded liaison with students, faculty and staff within that unit(s) to promote an environment that promotes student success and positive mental health. The SCC may also when appropriate provide mental health services including individual, couple, and group counseling and for providing psycho-educational programming and workshops to the campus community. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : 14 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Case Management/Care and Concern: 1. To work as part of the existing Care and Concern Network and provide intervention to students with appropriate referrals to campus and community resources as needed. 2. Engage with established referral structure and managing cases associated with college/dept through referral system and care and concern process. 3. Log referrals and student and faculty caseload into Maxient. 4. Determine needs for intervention, identification, and activation of appropriate resources and responses, ongoing monitoring, and evaluation of outcome and referrals. 5. Other duties as assigned. Outreach: 1. To serve as liaison with an academic college or department and other divisional offices. 2. To provide outreach programming to the university. 3. To provide consultation services and training to faculty and/or staff affiliated with the assigned college or department or administrative division. Therapy: 1. To provide individual, group, and couples counseling to MSU students. 2. To provide a rotating Counselor-on Duty response for urgent care between 8am and 5pm. 3. To share rotating evening and weekend emergency on-call response with other clinicians. 4. Maintain clinical case files in accordance with the highest legal, ethical, and professional standards when providing confidential clinical counseling. 5. To provide outreach, prevention, and consultation to students affiliated with an assigned college/department weekly. Supervisory Responsibility: This position reports jointly to the Director of Student Counseling Services (or their designee) in relation to mental health counseling services provided to clients as well as outreach activities and to the Dean of Students (or their designee) for the Case Management/Care and concern duties. The above essential duties are representative of major duties of positions in this position. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Other duties may be assigned to the above consistent with the knowledge, skills and abilities required for the job. Not all of the duties may be assigned to a position. Minimum Qualifications: Master's degree with a focus in mental health counseling, social work, or another licensed eligible mental health related field. Preferred Qualifications: Masters degree from an accredited institution of higher education in clinical mental health, social work, or a related field or PhD. in clinical or counseling psychology, clinical mental health or a related field from an accredited institution of higher education with 1 or more years of experience within a college counseling center. Licensure as a Licensed Professional Counselor, Licensed Social Worker or Licensed Psychologist or eligible to be licensed within 2 years in the state of Mississippi. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Experience helping student/individuals navigating life challenges. 2. Experience, knowledge and training in provision of individual, group and couple counseling. 3. Experience in provision of psycho-educational/outreach programming and workshops. 4. Experience with working with trauma related diagnoses. 5. Experience in provision of clinical services within a university counseling center preferred. 6. Ability to interact effectively and professionally with students. 7. Knowledge of and adherence to ethical standards endorsed by licensing professional organization. 8. Possess strong student orientation. 9. Motivated to function effectively with the organizational and administrative structure of a university. 10. Value involvement and participation within the Division of Student Affairs. 11. The ability to work with a diverse student population. 12. Ability to create and maintain, collegial, harmonious working relationships with others. Working Conditions and Physical Effort No unusual physical requirements. Requires no heavy lifting, and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. Frequent - Externally imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; travel or irregular hours often anticipated; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position; involves conflict-resolution or similar interactions involving emotional issues or stress on a regular basis Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands Job requires standing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 10 pounds Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2aca4315 Last Name (required) f62f2757 Email (required) 3c7b4437 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 3663904e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) eca81be0 Last Name (required) 4c30b76c Email (required) a4378107 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve 