    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/intermittent-worker-jackson-county-mississippi-united-states-8e234d32-6adf-4406-ba56-70f3c93e64c2": {
      "title": "Intermittent Worker",
      "description": "Intermittent Worker - Jackson County, Mississippi, United States Intermittent Worker - Jackson County, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Intermittent Worker 511089 Jackson County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 015900 - CREC-Coastal Research & Ext Center Intermittent Worker Support Staff Intermittent Opening on: Aug 11 2026 Position Function: Serves as a remote research assistant and is administratively associated with the MSU Coastal Research and Extension Center in support of its Experimental Seafood Processing Lab. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Mississippi State University’s Coastal Research and Extension Center in support of its Experimental Seafood Processing Lab (CREC-ESPL) is seeking an intermittent remote worker for automation production. This position is limited to working 720 hours within a fiscal year (July 1-June 30). Area of Specialization: Production Automation Anticipated Appointment Date: August 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Work in all phases of the development lifecycle, including requirements definition, software/systems design, implementation, testing, integration, and system support. 2. Integrate new image processing capabilities into automation production system, supported by AI/ML or classic image processing. 3. Collaborate with research staff and industry partners focused on both conventionally fabricated and additively manufactured materials and to assist with material qualification through computational modeling. 4. Primary areas of focus will be the modeling and analysis of materials and composite structures during a variety of manufacturing processes that may be mechanical, thermal, or electrical in nature. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor's degree. Preferred Qualifications: Master's degree. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Experience with additive manufacturing, image processing, programming (C++, python, etc.), and hardware setup, as required by the supervisor 2. Academic and/or work experience related to the field of research 3. Knowledge of research methods 4. Ability to work under pressure 5. Excellent time management skills Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. No unusual physical requirements. Requires limited lifting of files and records and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. 2. Frequent- External imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one's control; interruptions influence priorities; difficulty to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position; involves conflict-resolution or similar interactions involving emotion issues or stress on a regular basis. 3. Ability to occasionally work weekends and long hours. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online at www.jobs.msstate.edu by submitting a cover letter and curriculum vitae. Screening Date: August 18, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) aa8bfb23 Last Name (required) 6872ec5a Email (required) 9d25cd87 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 66d934a1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Intermittent Worker Support Staff Intermittent Worker Support Staff Employment Type Intermittent Intermittent Locations Jackson County, Mississippi, United States Jackson County, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) eb67a109 Last Name (required) 1b2d1985 Email (required) 1493fb2e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
