    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/resident-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-68f8c62d-577f-4cc9-b5e2-bb2f9d0b75d3": {
      "title": "Resident - Main Campus",
      "description": "Resident - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Resident - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Resident 511057 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 183900 - CVM Pathobiology/Population Med Dep Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Time-Limited Full-Time 12-Month Opening on: Aug 10 2026 Position Function: The Mississippi State University College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for a residency position in Veterinary Anatomic Pathology. The position is in the Department of Pathobiology and Population Medicine and the Diagnostic Laboratory Services (DLS), which is part of the Mississippi Veterinary Research and Diagnostic Laboratory System. This position is a 3-year residency training program that begins on July 1, 2027. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: Anatomical Pathology Essential Duties and Responsibilities: This post-DVM training program fulfills the residency training requirements for candidates seeking eligibility to take the certifying examinations of the American College of Veterinary Pathologists and is designed to prepare candidates for successful completion of those examinations. This residency is a three-year position that is renewable annually, subject to satisfactory performance. Residents work closely with 7 board-certified anatomic pathologists and 2 board-certified clinical pathologists. Training includes performing animal autopsies, reading surgical biopsies, teaching veterinary students in both didactic and clinical settings, and contributing case material to scholarly activities. The caseload is broad, with a notable proportion of domestic and farm animals. Diagnostic investigation is strongly supported, as are resident presentations and scientific publications. The program partners with the Institute for Marine Mammal Studies on the Gulf Coast of Mississippi, offering the potential to work with marine mammals if the candidate is interested. Two digital slide scanners are available for resident use: one at the Mississippi Veterinary Research and Diagnostic Laboratory in Pearl, MS, and the other at the Diagnostic and Aquatic Lab in the College of Veterinary Medicine in Starkville, MS. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include holding a DVM degree from an AVMA-accredited or listed veterinary school and obtaining veterinary licensure in Mississippi. Licensure in Mississippi requires passing the NAVLE exam before graduation. Veterinary students or Veterinarians who did not attend an AVMA-accredited veterinary school must also complete either the PAVE (Program for the Assessment of Veterinary Education Equivalence) or the ECFVG (Educational Commission for Foreign Veterinary Graduates) certification program. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong verbal and written communication skills, particularly in client service. Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, doctors, staff, and students to provide veterinary care and support the education of veterinary and veterinary technology students. Working Conditions and Physical Effort The job often involves walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, and handling objects with hands. It also requires standing, stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Complete applications are due by October 1, 2026, with invitations for virtual and/or on-site interviews to follow. Applicants should submit as part of the application package: Letter of application describing their interest and professional goals, Curriculum vitae, College transcripts (any social security numbers should be redacted from submitted transcripts), Three confidential letters of reference (at least one from a board-certified pathologist). Either the applicant or the referee can email the letters of reference. The selected candidate must report their NAVLE results (pass/fail) to the program cia email by April 1, 2027. The position will begin on July 1, 2027, with a starting salary of $45,000 per year. Please send questions and letters of reference to Peres Badial, DVM, PhD, DACVP (peres.badial@msstate.edu). Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 45b0702d Last Name (required) 1b7a3149 Email (required) bb3134a3 Refer someone to this job Apply Pl