    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/associate-professor-or-professor-and-head-riley-campus-meridian-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Professor or Professor and Head - Riley Campus",
      "description": "Associate Professor or Professor and Head - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Associate Professor or Professor and Head - Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate Professor or Professor and Head 511007 Riley Campus - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313223 - School of Health Professions Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Jul 27 2026 Position Function: The Department of Health Service Psychology in the School of Health Professions at Mississippi State University invites applications for a twelve-month administrative appointment as Associate or Full Professor & Head of the Department of Health Service Psychology. As a newly established department and school, we are dedicated to shaping the future of health service psychology, education and research. The Department of Health Services Psychology currently houses the Doctor of Psychology (PsyD) in Combined Health Service Psychology program and the MSU- Meridian Mental and Behavioral Health Clinic. We seek a dynamic and visionary leader with a strong academic and research background in health service psychology and with academic and/or clinical leadership experience to guide our department toward excellence. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: Health Service Psychology Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1) Provides vision and leadership for nationally recognized education and research programs 2) Provides leadership and mentoring to all faculty, staff and students 3) Responsible for overall administration of faculty and support staff activities 4) Responsible for recruitment of students, faculty and support staff 5) Provide oversight of the Mental & Behavioral Clinic, including supervision of clinical staff and the clinic director 6) Develop and implement strategic plans that advance clinic growth, sustainability, community impact, and operational excellence 7) Monitor clinic performance metrics, including client access, productivity, utilization, patient satisfaction, outcomes, and operational efficiency 8) Develop and maintain community partnerships that increase the clinic’s visibility, referral base, and service impact 9) Conducts research leading to scholarly publications 10) Works with the Dean of the School of Health Professions and university administration in establishing goals and objectives for the school, department, and in meeting the university missions of teaching, research and service 11) Academic responsibilities include planning, reviewing, and updating the curriculum, academic programs, and course content 12) Personnel responsibilities include promotion and tenure, performance evaluation, and workload management 13) Fiscal responsibilities include preparing and overseeing departmental budget and other budgets for research funding Minimum Qualifications: Doctorate degree in Clinical or Counseling Psychology or a closely related field from an APA-accredited program; Licensed or license-eligible as a Psychologist with the Mississippi Board of Psychology. Must qualify for the rank of Associate or Full Professor with tenure, and as such, must have earned national recognition by a distinguished record of accomplishments in teaching, research, and service. Preferred Qualifications: 1) Demonstrated leadership experience in an academic and clinical setting 2) Experience with accreditation processes, specifically APA 3) Proven ability to engage with healthcare industry stakeholders to foster partnerships and collaborative projects Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of Higher Education program development Working Conditions and Physical Effort Office Environment Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter, current curriculum vitae and the complete contact information for at least three professional references. Inquiries about the position may be directed to Lesley Clack, Dean, School of Health Professions, email lclack@meridian.msstate.edu or phone 601-696-2219 Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 30f48ff4 Last Name (required) 6122e449 Email (required) 22c3d0ec Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 06443cea Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Campus - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 71c5683d Last Name (required) 3964f28d Email (required) 19e9f248 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
