    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/graphic-designer-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Graphic Designer - Main Campus",
      "description": "Graphic Designer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Graphic Designer - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Graphic Designer 510988 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 441300 - MS State University Foundation Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Jul 27 2026 Position Function: The principal purpose this position is to provide graphic design, illustration, and print production for all major marketing and advertising pieces produced for the Division of Development and Alumni. Salary Grade : 13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure for salary ranges. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Implement design and creative direction of all marketing materials for the Division of Development and Alumni. 2. Collaborate with communication team members to achieve consistency in creative direction and design of external publications. This also includes working effectively with clients to translate their vision or need into an appropriate design that meets their marketing goal. 3. Design and produce high-quality marketing pieces that communicate a strategic university message to a broad audience in many different media formats (such as logos, stationary, brochures, direct mail solicitations, print ads, posters, newsletters, mailers, e­mail campaigns). 4. Successfully manage multiple projects concurrently, while meeting project budget and deadlines. Also, recording a daily status update for each of the projects within the project management system. 5. Coordinate print jobs with printing vendors. This includes coordination, job estimating, file preparation, packaging and shipping of files and proofs, and communicating revisions or approvals. 6. Foster an innovative and creative environment that is responsive to the needs of the division while ensuring that brand identity standards and brand personality are reflected in all communications. 7. Performs related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: - Bachelor's degree in Fine Arts or Graphic Design - Two years' experience Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Knowledge of principles and practices of graphic design • Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing • Ability to create and produce graphic materials using a range of media, methods, techniques, and equipment • Knowledge of graphic layout and photographic requirements and procedures • Skills in the utilization of specified computerized graphic design programs • Ability to analyze graphic and technical information and create interpretive illustrations • Budget development and management skills as related to the production of new digital or traditional media communications • Knowledge of printing procedures and requirements • Knowledge of printing and/or reproduction processes and techniques • Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to effectively communicate with a wide range of individuals and constituencies in a diverse community • Ability to analyze and interpret user graphic requirements • Ability to develop print and/or reproduction specifications Working Conditions and Physical Effort • No unusual physical requirements. Requires limited lifting of files and records and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. • Frequent- External imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one's control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position; involves conflict-resolution or similar interactions involving emotional issues or stress on a regular basis. • Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. Instructions for Applying: Submit an online application along with a resume and cover letter. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b2a34d78 Last Name (required) a7af3585 Email (required) 04bd96c7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert c32dd97f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 60286e2c Last Name (required) a7b27669 Email (required) 65659f75 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
