    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/intermittent-worker-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-42276239-b39e-4f7d-b794-c47809e8f5b5": {
      "title": "Intermittent Worker - Main Campus",
      "description": "Intermittent Worker - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Intermittent Worker - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Intermittent Worker 510968 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 182000 - Department of Comparative Bio Scien Intermittent Worker Intermittent Opening on: Jul 17 2026 Position Function: The function of the Intermittent Worker is to provide administrative support and coordinate the administrative function of the Nancy Fair Link Laminitis Research Center. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: Laminitis Research Center Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Provides administrative support to the Nancy Fair Link Laminitis Research Center, including preparation, editing, and maintenance of correspondence, reports, spreadsheets, databases, and other administrative documents. 2. Assists with budget monitoring and financial administration by tracking expenditures, maintaining budget records, compiling financial data, and preparing summary reports for the Center Director. 3. Coordinates procurement activities, including preparation and processing of purchase requests, orders, payments, reimbursements, and acquisition of supplies, equipment, and services in accordance with University policies. 4. Reconciles procurement card (ProCard), travel, and other financial transactions; assists with monthly and annual financial reviews, audits, and supporting documentation. 5. Coordinates travel arrangements and travel reimbursements for Center personnel using University-approved systems and procedures. 6. Maintains administrative records, databases, inventories, and filing systems; ensures accuracy, organization, and compliance with University record-retention requirements. 7. Assists with inventory management, including equipment tracking, inventory audits, asset documentation, and surplus or disposal processes. 8. Coordinates meetings, workshops, seminars, and other Center activities, including scheduling, calendar management, preparation of meeting materials, and recording meeting minutes. 9. Serves as a liaison between the Center and University administrative offices, including Human Resources, Procurement, Accounting, Sponsored Programs, and College administration. 10. Assists with personnel-related administrative processes, including timesheet management, leave processing, payroll documentation, onboarding paperwork, and other routine human resources functions. 11. Collects, compiles, and summarizes operational data to support Center reporting, planning, and decision-making activities. 12. Performs other administrative and operational duties as assigned in support of the mission and activities of the Nancy Fair Link Laminitis Research Center. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High school diploma Experience: Two (2) years of clerical or office experience directly related to the duties and responsibilities specified. When a candidate has the required education, but lacks the required experience, they may normally apply additional appropriate education toward the experience requirement, at a rate of one (1) year relevant education per year of required experience. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Bachelor’s degree in accounting or business. 2. Experience in fund accounting. 3. Experience with the MSU Banner Operating System. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Demonstrated computer literacy skills, using MS Office applications and other basic data systems including internet navigation, maintenance skills. 2. Organizing and coordinating skills. 3. Ability to manage their time and tasks effectively and efficiently, handling multiple time sensitive projects at the same time. 4. Ability to maintain confidentiality of records and information. 5. Ability to perform simple accounting procedures. 6. Ability to understand and follow specific instructions and procedures. 7. Ability to maintain calendars and schedule appointments. 8. Ability to create, compose, and edit written materials. 9. Knowledge of supplies, equipment, and/or services ordering and inventory control. 10. Skill in the use of operating basic office equipment. 11. Ability to communicate effectively, both orally and in writing. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Work is normally performed in a typical interior/office work environment. 2. No or very limited exposure to physical risk. 3. Limited physical effort required. 4. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include a cover letter and resume along with names and addresses of at least three references. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2571890a Last Name (required) 165808a1 Email (required) 3cc3add4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert af33dad3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Intermittent Worker Intermittent Worker Employment Type Intermittent Intermittent Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 0e9b59ee Last Name (required) 8f68f2f0 Email (required) 999ec761 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
