    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/agricultural-technician-pearl-river-county-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Agricultural Technician",
      "description": "Agricultural Technician - Pearl River County, Mississippi, United States Agricultural Technician - Pearl River County, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Agricultural Technician 510903 Pearl River County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 013000 - CREC-So MS Branch Exp Station Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Jul 13 2026 Position Function: Performs farm related or agricultural essential technical tasks at an agriculture research/teaching facility. Salary Grade : 10 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Coastal Research and Extension Center serves as Mississippi State University's 'southern exposure'. CREC-White Sand unit is the headquarters of our beef cattle program. Area of Specialization: Beef Cattle Anticipated Appointment Date: August 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Perform daily care and management of beef cattle, including feeding, watering, health observations, and moving animals between pastures and facilities. • Safely handle cattle during routine management procedures, including weighing, vaccinations, deworming, pregnancy diagnosis, artificial insemination support, ear tagging, blood collection assistance, and other research-related activities. • Operate and maintain agricultural equipment, including tractors, skid steers, utility vehicles, mowers, hay equipment, and other farm machinery. • Assist with hay and forage production, including mowing, raking, baling, hauling, storing hay, and pasture maintenance. • Construct, repair, and maintain fences, gates, corrals, water systems, and other farm infrastructure. • Maintain barns, working facilities, equipment, and research areas to ensure a safe and functional work environment. • Assist with implementation of research projects by collecting samples, recording data accurately, and following experimental protocols. • Transport livestock, feed, equipment, and supplies as needed. • Perform routine maintenance and minor repairs on farm equipment and facilities. • Follow all animal welfare, biosafety, and workplace safety protocols. • Work outdoors in varying weather conditions and perform physically demanding tasks, including lifting heavy materials, walking long distances, and handling livestock. • Perform other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma and six months of experience directly related to the duties and responsibilities specified AND six months of general experience. Preferred Qualifications: BS in Agricultural Science Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Experience handling beef cattle using low-stress livestock handling techniques. • Ability to safely operate tractors and other agricultural equipment. • Experience with fence construction and repair. • Knowledge of pasture and forage management practices. • Basic mechanical skills for equipment maintenance and troubleshooting. • Ability to safely operate trailers and transport livestock (preferred). • Ability to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a research team. • Ability to lift at least 50 lb and perform strenuous physical labor. • Valid driver’s license with an acceptable driving record. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting, bending or other physical exertion. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. Routine deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires standing, walking, sitting, reaching, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Job occasionally requires working on weekends. Job occasionally requires climbing or balancing, and lifting more than 100 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Please apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Screening Date: July 20, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) f9f9bd14 Last Name (required) 6673d03f Email (required) 40adfdb9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
