    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/sound-technician-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-13c84beb-ea59-4939-84c0-41fd530ff197": {
      "title": "Sound Technician - Main Campus",
      "description": "Sound Technician - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Sound Technician - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Sound Technician 510821 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 540100 - Colvard Student Union Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Jun 15 2026 Position Function: Work involves the installation, operation, modification, maintenance, and repair of a variety of sound devices and audio equipment in regards to facilities and special events. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: Event Services Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Responsible for setting up, adjusting, and running audio equipment for University events such as inaugurations, commencements, concerts, sporting events, etc. 2. Conducts field repairs on equipment as necessary. 3. Serves as a quick responder to events where there are problems with equipment. 4. Maintains required performance and maintenance records for sound equipment. 5. Responsible for maintaining audio equipment inventory. 6. Travels to off-campus locations to set up and operate sound equipment for University related events. 7. Provides support and services to administration and University constituents as needed. 8. Will be required to work evenings and weekends to provide services at after-hours events. 9. Perform related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1. High School diploma or equivalent. 2. Three to five years of related experience. -or- Any equivalent combination of related experience and/or education approved by the Department of Human Resources Management. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Additional college or technical education in a related field. 2. Experience with sound, lighting and video systems Working Conditions and Physical Effort This position requires the employee to perform physical duties including working at varying heights and ability to lift, and/or carry, equipment weighing up to 100 pounds. Instructions for Applying: Submit application online with a resume and a list of three references. Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 4bbcaad9 Last Name (required) e3156d57 Email (required) 73f9c112 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert a6e04246 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) e8c5fb45 Last Name (required) 21adc977 Email (required) 0f35c634 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
