    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-2debe7f4-e7b3-4c3c-82e3-f79de070df51": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Teaching Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Teaching Professor 510772 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 051700 - Department of Kinesiology Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Jun 26 2026 Position Function: The Department of Kinesiology at Mississippi State University is seeking applications for a nine-month, non-tenure track faculty position as an Assistant Teaching Professor starting in August 2026. A doctorate in Exercise Science or related science discipline is required. The preferred candidate must be able to teach anatomical kinesiology, applied anatomy and pathophysiology, medical terminology, and other relevant courses. Candidates who are ABD will be considered at the instructor level with completion required within one year from date of hire. Promotion to Assistant Teaching Professor will occur when degree requirements are completed. Evaluation of applications is ongoing and will continue until the position is filled. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The department of Kinesiology is housed within the College of Education and has over 20 faculty serving approximately 1,100 graduate and undergraduate students. In August 2025, the department moved into a brand new, state-of-the-art facility with over 16,000 square feet of research space, classrooms, and offices. Undergraduate students choose from among six concentrations: Sport Administration, Clinical Exercise Physiology, Neuromechanics, Physical Activity and Coaching, Physical Education and Coaching, and Strength and Conditioning. Master's students have four concentrations to choose from: Sport Administration, Sport Pedagogy, Disability Studies, and Exercise Physiology. Doctoral students choose between Sport Studies and Exercise Science. For more than 15 years, the Department of Kinesiology has consistently maintained an undergraduate population exceeding 1,000 students. Recent data indicate interest in the field will continue to grow. Over the past three academic years, the department has enrolled its largest freshman class on record, culminating in fall 2025 with 305 students, the highest to date. These trends reflect strong and consistent student interest in Kinesiology at the undergraduate level. At present, the department has prioritized course access for Kinesiology majors, and as a result, the immediate impact on these students has been minimized. However, non-Kinesiology majors have experienced limited access to courses because of their delayed ability to register and often have to take online courses because face-to-face options have reached capacity. This position will help the department more easily accommodate students in other programs whose degree pathways rely on Kinesiology courses, particularly those in pre-health, BSIS, nutrition, and related fields. Area of Specialization: Exercise Science Anticipated Appointment Date: August 16, 2026 Tenure Track Status: Non-Tenure Track Essential Duties and Responsibilities: --High commitment to quality teaching at the undergraduate, and potentially graduate, level. Courses taught will include, but not be limited to, anatomical kinesiology, applied anatomy and pathophysiology, and medical terminology. --Service involvement in the Department of Kinesiology, the College of Education, Mississippi State University, the wider community, and the field of Kinesiology --Counsel students on career direction --Other duties as required Minimum Qualifications: --Doctoral degree in Exercise Science or related field --ABD will be considered at the instructor level with completion required within one year of hiring --Demonstrated potential to teach at the college level --Comprehensive knowledge of human anatomy, physiology, pathophysiology, and medical terminology Preferred Qualifications: --Prior undergraduate and graduate teaching experience. --Experience with online teaching, as well as course and program development. --Experience with course and program development Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: --Ability to work as a member of a multidisciplinary department is desirable. --Excellent interpersonal and communication skills are required. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Standard office and professional environment Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ --Applicant must apply online. --Please include cover letter and CV along with names and addresses of three references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) b1605490 Last Name (required) 9e3dc57e Email (required) 30bdd72d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 0d5be8a4 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 9-month Regular Full-Time 9-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 89dfff4b Last Name (required) f83b4783 Email (required) c19cb489 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others he