    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/lead-irrigation-technician-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Lead Irrigation Technician - Main Campus",
      "description": "Lead Irrigation Technician - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Lead Irrigation Technician - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Lead Irrigation Technician 510525 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 751400 - Campus Landscape Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Apr 27 2026 Position Function: Manages the repairs, installation and maintenance on all irrigation systems associated with the University. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Manages the installation and maintenance of the irrigation systems, ensuring work is completed according to established plans and standards 2. Performs seasonal irrigation services: Spring start-ups, winterization/turn-offs and mid-season checks. 3. - Provides input and support on the layout and setup of university irrigation systems to achieve efficient and uniform distribution of water. 4. Operates machinery/equipment such as a tractor, dozer, skidsteer, and trencher if needed. 5. Installs, connects, programs, and repairs wiring, valves, sprinkler heads and electronic controllers, ensuring all are functioning properly and without fault. 6. Performs preventative and routine maintenance on irrigation systems. 7. Cleans and services fountains on campus. 8. Manages and installs outdoor lighting as necessary. 9. Monitor supply levels and reports material or equipment needs to supervisor. May assist in other general campus landscape duties when needed, such as laying sod, planting trees/shrubbery, and mowing campus grounds. 10. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervisory Responsibility: Supervises and trains team members when needed Minimum Qualifications: Education High School diploma or equivalent Experience 5 years of experience in landscape construction, irrigation installation, and/or landscape management. Substitutions Any equivalent combination of related experience and/or education approved by the Department of Human Resources Management. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Ability to read basic blueprints and understand site layout. • Skilled in the use of irrigation tools, controllers, valves, and related equipment. • Ability to safely operate heavy equipment such as tractors, skid steers, and trenchers. • Knowledge of common plant materials and landscape practices. • Strong communication and teamwork skills. • Ability to follow detailed instructions and support crew organization. • Problem-solving skills related to irrigation and landscaping tasks. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting, bending or other physical exertion. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. Routine deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; travel or other inconveniences have advance notice; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires standing, walking, reaching, climbing or balancing, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Job occasionally requires sitting, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting more than 100 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online and complete a support staff application. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) ab2f8a33 Last Name (required) 27e9eda2 Email (required) e6afff60 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert d75ca434 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 42aa2dba Last Name (required) 4c8f846f Email (required) 61bcdde6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
