    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/agricultural-technician-stoneville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Agricultural Technician",
      "description": "Agricultural Technician - Stoneville, MS, Mississippi, United States Agricultural Technician - Stoneville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Agricultural Technician 510518 Stoneville, MS Mississippi - Not located on main campus 013200 - Delta Research and Extension Center Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: May 7 2026 Position Function: Perform routine and specialized procedures in support of research projects. Salary Grade : 10 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: This position will be located at the Delta Research and Extension Center in Stoneville, MS. Area of Specialization: Catfish Farm Anticipated Appointment Date: June 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Conduct field and laboratory activities in support of research, such as feeding fish in specific ponds a variety of diets using hydraulic fish feeders with digital scales, recording feed data, weighing feed and fish, harvesting and sampling fish, measuring fish, counting fish, collecting water samples, measuring water quality, and fertilizing ponds. 2. Assist in field operations such as pond maintenance; perform general clean up of facilities and equipment as requested. 3. Assist with data collection and tabulation as needed. 4. Maintain and operate pumps and wells to supply water to tanks and ponds 5. Maintain, calibrate, and operate a variety of dissolved oxygen monitoring equipment 6. Perform related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High school diploma or GED. Experience (yrs.): Six months of experience directly related to the duties and responsibilities specified AND six months of general experience. Certifications and/or Licensures: 1. Valid driver’s license. 2. Must obtain a Certified Pesticide Applicators Certificate within 90 days of employment or complete the worker/handler training, whichever is applicable. Substitution allowed: Any equivalent education and/or experience will be considered. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to follow instructions. Knowledge of agricultural processes. Good communications skills. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Ability to work in extreme weather conditions. 2. Ability to work after normal hours during peak season will be required Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. For additional questions, please contact Billy Rutland, brutland@drec.msstate.edu, 662-686-3325 Screening Date: May 14, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 5bbfd28c Last Name (required) 9bacc325 Email (required) e99feb3d Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 374c76d6 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Stoneville, MS, Mississippi, United States Stoneville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 9d3bbcd2 Last Name (required) e3a4a4b0 Email (required) da5849ca Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank y