    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/extension-program-assistant-harrison-county-mississippi-united-states-7feee63f-1e57-4ff7-995a-eb0462e8f162": {
      "title": "Extension Program Assistant",
      "description": "Extension Program Assistant - Harrison County, Mississippi, United States Extension Program Assistant - Harrison County, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Extension Program Assistant 510440 Harrison County Mississippi - Not located on main campus 015901 - CREC-Coastal Marine Ext Program Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Apr 24 2026 Position Function: To support a variety of routine and specialized Extension and research duties focused on a combination of coastal conservation and restoration, environmental monitoring, environmental stewardship, and environmental education. This position is administratively associated with the MSU Coastal Research and Extension Center in support of its Coastal and Marine Extension Program (CREC-CMEP). Salary Grade : 08 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Mississippi State University’s Coastal Research and Extension Center in support of its Coastal and Marine Extension Program (CREC-CMEP) is seeking a Extension Program Assistant to support a variety of routine and specialized Extension and research duties focused on a combination of coastal conservation and restoration, environmental monitoring, environmental stewardship, and environmental education. This position will be administratively housed in the Coastal and Marine Extension Program located at the Coastal Research and Extension Center in Biloxi, MS. Anticipated Appointment Date: May 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The selected applicant will become part of the Coastal and Marine Extension Program (CMEP) and will be involved with a variety of program activities. The primary activities for the selected applicant are outlined below but could include any activities associated with the Coastal and Marine Extension Program. The primary focus of the selected applicant will be to assist with research, outreach, and training related to coastal conservation and restoration, resilience, sustainability, marine debris/litter reduction, and other duties as assigned. The primary responsibilities of the selected applicant will be to lead and/or assist with the development, implementation, and evaluation of activities emphasized above. These duties will include activities such as, but not limited to: * Organizing routine meetings with participants, partners, and team members; * Leading and/or co-leading workshops for project participants and engaging in outreach opportunities. * Leading and assisting with the preparation and dissemination of outreach materials, Extension publications, and technical reports; * Applying for and managing extramural funding; * Collecting, interpreting, and reporting data; * Performing research activities, such as literature reviews and sample collection/processing; * Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications: High school diploma. Preferred Qualifications: * Experience, preferably in community engagement and/or education; * Extension, applied research, outreach, education, and project management experience; * Familiarity with coastal, marine, and estuarine ecosystems and associated field research. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: * Must have reliable personal transportation, a valid driver’s license, and ability to travel often to sites along coastal MS, AL, and FL; * Ability to develop and maintain diverse and robust partnerships; * Typing and computer skills (word processing and spreadsheets); * Highly flexible: ability to adapt to a rapidly changing schedule; * Ability to juggle multiple tasks and prioritize multiple demands; * Strong oral and written communication skills; * Knowledge and skills in using Microsoft Office Suites especially Word, Excel, PowerPoint; knowledge and skills in document/project management/sharing platforms (e.g. Google Drive, Basecamp, etc.); * Ability to apply for, secure, and manage extramural funding. Working Conditions and Physical Effort * Ability to work in extreme weather conditions for extended periods of time; * Ability to work long hours, occasionally in remote locations; * Requires substantial routine travel, including overnight trips Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.jobs.msstate.edu by submitting a professional staff application along with a cover letter, resume, and academic transcripts into the online portal. Any social security numbers included on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online. Screening Date: May 1, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) ff1e48aa Last Name (required) ba4a79a1 Email (required) 815c50fc Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 4417498c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Harrison County, Mississippi, United States Harrison County, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 20e73595 Last Name (required) b9a42a72 Email (required) 51157a