    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/print-manager-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Print Manager - Main Campus",
      "description": "Print Manager - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Print Manager - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Print Manager 510406 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011000 - Agricultural Communications Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Apr 9 2026 Position Function: Oversees the daily operations and function of the Extension Print and Publications Supply area for Mississippi State University Extension Service. Salary Grade : 14 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Office of Agricultural Communications provides communications, leadership, products and services for the MSU Extension Service and the Division of Agriculture, Forestry & Veterinary Medicine and select organizations. Our personnel include Photographers, Videographers, Social Media, Graphic Designers and a Print Shop. Anticipated Appointment Date: May 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The Print Manager is responsible for the effective and efficient management of the Extension Print Shop, Publications & Supply Distribution, AV Reference Room, and Extension warehouse and serves as Extension Mail Officer. The Print Manager will have management responsibilities for all employees and equipment within those functions. The manager assures those functions provide timely turnaround of job orders and requests. The manager is responsible for planning the acquisition of all supplies and materials, maintenance contracts, and the replacement and upgrade of equipment for those areas. The manager will work with the Head of Agricultural Communications in planning for the future of the Print Shop and ways to increase service and value to our internal customers. The manager works closely with others in Agricultural Communications and coordinates with professionals at the state, regional, and county levels of the Extension organization. The manager must be competent in cost estimation, charge back systems, printing and related technology and techniques, equipment operation, and other aspects of the profession. The manager represents the organization at technical conferences and other printing association meetings held at local, regional, and national levels. The manager also represents the organization at in-service training sessions held for Extension employees. The manager maintains administration of the online store/ordering system for the Print Shop (currently Pressero) and the Inventory Control Management system & Print on Demand (currently Oracle). The manager is the Project Coordinator for all Print Shop projects using project management software (Currently Workzone). This includes communication with clients and potential clients, accepting jobs, timing of accepted jobs, obtaining billing information, ensuring correct invoicing/billing of the completed jobs, and updating the project status. The manager reports to the Head of Agricultural Communications and interfaces daily with supervisors and employees of other support units and Division of Agriculture departments. Supervisory Responsibility Full supervisory responsibility for other employees is a major responsibility and includes training, evaluating performance, and making or recommending pay, promotion or other employment decisions. The above essential duties are representative of major duties in this position. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Other duties may be assigned to the above consistent with the knowledge, skills and abilities required for the job. Not all of the duties may be assigned to a position. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s Degree in Management, Journalism, Communication, Marketing, Public Relations, or related field Experience: Four (4) years of experience in print shop operations including customer service An equivalent combination of related education and related experience may be considered for this position. Preferred Qualifications: Experience spec’ing and estimating jobs for printing/duplication. Knowledge of paper and other consumables. Shipping/mailing experience. Experience in University-wide Banner reporting system Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong Background in Management- specifically Project Management, Billing, Invoicing Previous computer-related experience. Strong customer-service skills. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Occasional and/or light lifting required. Limited exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc., but none to the point of being disagreeable. May involve minor safety hazards where likely result would be cuts, bruises, etc. Routine deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires standing, walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, . Job occasionally requires climbing or balancing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, handling objects with hands, and lifting up to 50 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically, ability to distinguish colors. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ To apply, please complete the online application and attach a cover letter and resume' Screening Date: April 23, 2026, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) bfd0f809 Last Name (required) 24b70bce Email (required) d162d017 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert c0c1c4ae Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 06d87792 Last Name (required) 8ceda039 Email (required) 3af5d3de Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
