    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/intermittent-worker-clinic-nurse-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Intermittent Worker- Clinic Nurse - Main Campus",
      "description": "Intermittent Worker- Clinic Nurse - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Intermittent Worker- Clinic Nurse - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Intermittent Worker- Clinic Nurse 510160 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 560117 - SHC - Clinical Care Intermittent Worker Intermittent Opening on: Jan 14 2026 Position Function: Provides general medical care to patients, within the scope of applicable licensure, as directed by clinicians of the John C. Longest Student Health Center. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The following examples are intended as illustrations only of the various types of duties assigned in positions allocated to this classification. The absence of specific statements of duties does not exclude those tasks from the position if the work is similar, related, or a logical assignment of the position. 1. Provides direct patient care including: a. Gathers medical history from patient. b. Interviews patients, measures vital signs and records information in patient's chart. c. Prepares examination rooms for patients. d. Assists clinicians with examinations. e. Conducts vision and hearing tests. f. Changes dressings, administers IV's, medications, and injections if within scope of license. g. Performs PEAK tests and administers nebulizer treatment. h. Performs x-ray procedures per established protocols and training. 2. Performs miscellaneous duties including: a. Makes referral appointments for patients. b. Calls in prescriptions to pharmacies, faxes reports to others doctors and to hospitals. c. Maintains inventory of supplies, restocks examination rooms and trauma room with instruments and other supplies. d. Maintains current BLS and OSHA certifications, participates in assessment and quality improvement programs. 3. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: At least one year experience as a nurse in a clinical setting. Current Mississippi license as a Registered Nurse. Degree from an accredited nursing program. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Work experience above the minimum required performing related duties. 2. Certification in ACLS, college health nursing, or office x-ray. 3. BSN degree. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: 1. Ability to prioritize competing demands and to meet deadlines. 2. Ability to work independently and as a member of a team. 3. Ability to exercise good judgment and discipline. 4. Strong verbal, written communication, and interpersonal skills. 5. Ability to work in a diverse environment. 6. Ability to efficiently and effectively work in a fast-paced environment with multiple responsibilities. 7. Ability to foster teamwork with willingness to demonstrate life-long learning for professional growth as a medical professional. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. General office conditions. 2. Exposure to communicable diseases, body fluids, blood and blood products. 3. Potential for injury from needles and other sharp objects. 4. Potential for injury from chemicals. 5. Possible exposure to radiation from x-ray. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Please complete the online application and provide cover letter and resume. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 0aaf0cdd Last Name (required) 1880fda7 Email (required) 36726360 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert bc1ec372 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Intermittent Worker Intermittent Worker Employment Type Intermittent Intermittent Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 1239fa78 Last Name (required) 19c371ae Email (required) e053cde8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
