    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-a655adbe-06cc-4eb5-ba7b-7d93cd0c24ce": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant or Associate Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant or Associate Professor 509987 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 012100 - School of Human Sciences Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Dec 15 2025 Position Function: Facilitate Extension program planning, evaluation, and staff development processes. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The School of Human Sciences provides education, research, and outreach programs related to human interaction and relationships, early childhood, child life, youth, adult and family studies, and teacher education in Family and Consumer Sciences and Agricultural Education. In addition, selected School programs focus on commerce, marketing, and using technology for problem-solving and designing programs and projects. MSU Extension’s Program and Staff Development team, also located in the School, is dedicated to building the professional, programmatic, and evaluation knowledge and capacity of MSU Extension professionals. Area of Specialization: Ag Education, Leadership, and Communications – Extension Program and Staff Development Anticipated Appointment Date: July 1, 2026. Tenure Track Status: Yes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Facilitate Extension program planning, evaluation, and staff development processes. • Consult with Extension faculty and implement program planning and evaluation efforts. • Develop educational materials and publications related to Extension program development, planning, and evaluation, and staff development. • Coordinate in-service educational programs related to program development, planning, and evaluation, and staff development for Extension field staff and faculty. • Use effective verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills and techniques to build and maintain relationships with Extension professionals at county, state, regional, and national levels. • Provide nonformal education through distance education methods (e.g., Canvas, Zoom, Teams). • Maintain a program of scholarship (i.e., research) related to Extension program and staff development. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Qualifications for Assistant Professor: • Earned doctorate in Extension education or a related field (ABD will be considered) • Experience in Extension, teaching, research, or a related area Minimum Qualifications for Associate Professor: • Earned doctorate in Extension education or a related field • Experience in Extension, teaching, research, or a related area • Awarded or pending tenure at a comparable university or have at least four years of experience and an outstanding record of scholarly productivity ABDs or degree pending considered (all but DISS): Yes. Preferred Qualifications: • Evidence of computer/technology skills, including distance education • Ability to interpret research and technical information for the public • Evidence of success in competitive extramural funding • Evidence of conducting research through design, implementation, and evaluation Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Please refer to above Working Conditions and Physical Effort None Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.jobs.msstate.edu Please include a letter of application including cover letter outlining Extension, research, and teaching expertise, curriculum vitae, transcripts of graduate courses with SSN redacted, and name, address, telephone number, and email address of three professional references. Review of applications will continue until the position is filled. Screening Date: December 29, 2025, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 6c30fb0b Last Name (required) 8143e15e Email (required) 29b85e0a Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 2b4f8003 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) d0d06c66 Last Name (required) c07f6aec Email (required) 21ab5661 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
