    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/intermittent-worker-raymond-ms-mississippi-united-states-93ee8882-21e9-4544-b1f1-e0aff17e6e50": {
      "title": "Intermittent Worker",
      "description": "Intermittent Worker - Raymond, MS, Mississippi, United States Intermittent Worker - Raymond, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Intermittent Worker 509404 Raymond, MS Mississippi - Not located on main campus 015700 - Central MS Research & Ext Center Intermittent Worker Support Staff Intermittent Opening on: Jul 10 2025 Position Function: This position performs a variety of basic facilities and grounds support at CMREC, the Brown Loam Branch Experiment Station in Raymond, and the Truck Crops Branch Experiment Station in Crystal Springs. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Central Mississippi Research and Extension Center (CMREC) is one of four Research and Extension Centers in the MSU System and located in Raymond, MS. Area of Specialization: Facilities/Grounds Anticipated Appointment Date: August 2025. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Assist with general building maintenance and upkeep, including but not limited to pressure washing, painting, minor repairs, and cleaning. 2. Assist with general landscaping maintenance and upkeep, including but not limited to mowing, weed eating, fencing, limb/debris pickup and removal, painting, and minor repairs. 3. Assist in cleaning and servicing University vehicles and equipment. 4. Assist in moving equipment and non-hazardous materials. 5. Assists with feeding farm animals. 6. Assists with event setup and take-down as needed. Minimum Qualifications: Education: High school education or GED. Licensure: Must have a valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Farm-related work experience beyond the minimum required. 2. Previous experience with farm and/or facilities operations. 3. Previous experience with landscaping. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Mechanical and technical skills related to essential duties and responsibilities. Ability to follow directions, get along well with others, and meet supervisor expectations. Ability to travel to multiple sites in a University vehicle. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. Ability to work in extreme weather conditions. 2. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing, or pulling required of objects up to 50 pounds. 3. Will operate and work in close proximity with heavy farm equipment. 4. Possible contact with herbicides and pesticides. 5. Must be comfortable working around farm animals. 6. Must be willing to occasionally work assignments outside of normal business hours to include weekend hours. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Submit application and any requested documents online. All applicants must apply online at www.jobs.msstate.edu and provide the complete contact information for at least three references. Call Dr. Curt Lacy at (601) 857-2284 for additional information. Screening Date: July 17, 2025, until filled. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) a129ddce Last Name (required) a8249d42 Email (required) 969ec312 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Research Technician Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The research technician will work directly with team leads, undergraduate students and/or recent graduates, and federal and state conservation partners in the southeastern region to review state and regional conservation planning documents and populate and deploy advanced data applications focused on prioritized species conservation and habitat recovery efforts. Clinical Laboratory Manager ***Internal Posting*** Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Directs and coordinates activities of employees engaged in performing laboratory tests to obtain data for use in diagnosis and treatment of diseases. Also performs duties of Medical Technologist. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 840521c2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Intermittent Worker Support Staff Intermittent Worker Support Staff Employment Type Intermittent Intermittent Locations Raymond, MS, Mississippi, United States Raymond, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) f2f881f7 Last Name (required) 2c0bb7fd Email (required) 39dc01d0 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
