    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-head-center-for-4-h-youth-development-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development - Main Campus",
      "description": "Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development 511373 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 013600 - Ctr 4-H Youth Development Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Oct 16 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Assistant Head of 4-H at the MSUES Center for 4-H Youth Development provides leadership and administrative support for statewide 4-H youth development initiatives. This position is responsible for program planning, implementation, evaluation, and compliance across all major 4-H program areas. The Assistant Head works collaboratively with Extension faculty, staff, and volunteers to ensure high-quality, research-based youth programming that aligns with organizational goals and federal and state requirements. This is a 12-month position that reports directly to the Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development. Salary Grade : 17 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Anticipated Appointment Date: December 2026. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Provide leadership for the development, coordination, and evaluation of statewide 4-H programs, events, and initiatives. • Assist the State 4-H Program Leader in strategic planning, policy development, and program administration. • Support county Extension personnel through training, coaching, and resource development. • Ensure program compliance with federal, state, and university policies, including youth protection, risk management, and reporting requirements. • Oversee program quality assurance processes, including data collection, evaluation, and impact reporting. • Coordinate development and dissemination of 4-H curricula, educational materials, and professional development resources. • Strengthen volunteer systems, including recruitment, onboarding, training, and recognition. • Develop and maintain partnerships with schools, community organizations, agencies, and stakeholders to expand program reach. • Assist with grant development, budget planning, and resource allocation to support statewide programming. • Represent the 4-H program at state, regional, and national meetings assigned. • Serve as acting State 4-H Program Leader in their absence. • Performs other duties as assigned. The above essential duties are representative of major duties in this position. Specific duties and responsibilities may vary based upon departmental needs. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Master’s degree in youth development, education, leadership development, agriculture, family and consumer sciences, Extension education, or a closely related field. Experience: Five (5) years demonstrated experience in youth development, leadership development, and administrative leadership including supervision, program management, or organizational leadership. Preferred Qualifications: • Doctoral degree in youth development, education, leadership development, agriculture, family and consumer sciences, Extension education, or a closely related field. • Significant administrative leadership experience in an educational, youth-serving, or community-based organization. • Experience in personnel management, performance evaluation, conflict management, and employee development. • Experience applying disciplinary procedures and enforcing organizational policies. • Experience leading organizational change and implementing strategic initiatives. • Experience managing budgets, grants, and fiscal compliance. • Experience working with Extension, K-12, higher education, or youth development environments. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Ability to manage multiple projects and deadlines. • Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. • Proficiency in program evaluation and reporting. • Ability to develop and deliver training and professional development. • Effective leadership and team-building skills. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Ability and willingness to travel frequently within the state and occasionally out of state to support statewide programming, training, and events. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Must complete online application; submit a cover letter, resume, three professional references, and a current unofficial transcript. Please note that any social security number included on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online and that official transcripts will be requested of finalists. Screening Date: October 30, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) cfb96afe Last Name (required) f5678130 Email (required) 20dc4db4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Intermittent Worker Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi These positions will assist the Purchasing area of the College of Veterinary Medicine Photographer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The photographer works to expand the state, regional and national visibility of Mississippi State University through conceiving, executing and delivering high-quality, professional images that align with the university mission and the current branding campaign. The photographer covers all areas of the university, including a variety of indoor and outdoor events, some of which require availability outside regular work hours and minimal travel. Photographic collaboration with the support of all campus partners is expected. Extension Agent Walthal County, Mississippi Responsible for providing leadership in the development, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive non-formal, experiential educational program in the area of positive youth development (4-H). The Extension Agent serves as a member of the county team to determine effective programming priorities and delivery methods for the community. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert b1b80edd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (requi