    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/intermittent-worker-riley-center-meridian-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Intermittent Worker - Riley Center",
      "description": "Intermittent Worker - Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Intermittent Worker - Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Intermittent Worker 508902 Riley Center - Meridian, MS Mississippi - Meridian Campus 313214 - MSU-Riley Center Intermittent Worker Intermittent Opening on: Mar 3 2025 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: This position will provide intermittent assistance to conference and events team and/or management at the Riley Center in Meridian. Employees hired into Intermittent positions are limited to working no more than 720 hours per fiscal year. Salary Grade : UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Mississippi State University Riley Center is a Performing Arts and Conference Center that opened in 2006 in Meridian, Mississippi. We host more than 25 performing arts events as well as over 100 conference events each year. Visit www.msurileycenter.com for more information. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: *Must be able to regularly lift and transport equipment weighing up to 75 pounds. *Assist the Events Manager and team with on-site setup for Riley Center events. *Ensure that all setups are accurate according to provided layout diagrams. *Conduct setup evaluations with Events Manager upon completion of duties. *Help to ensure that all event setup times are met according to weekly schedule. *Follow proper procedures to ensure personal safety and the security of the venue's physical resources. Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent Two years of related experience - or - Any equivalent combination of related experience and/or education approved by the Department of Human Resources Management Working Conditions and Physical Effort *Physical effort required. *Considerable physical activity. Requires heavy physical work; heavy lifting, pushing, or pulling is required of objects up to 75 pounds. Physical work is a primary part (more than 70%) of the job. Instructions for Applying: Applicant must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 82655c01 Last Name (required) 52c19b1c Email (required) 948511d7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Intermittent Worker Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi These positions will assist the Purchasing area of the College of Veterinary Medicine Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Assistant Head of 4-H at the MSUES Center for 4-H Youth Development provides leadership and administrative support for statewide 4-H youth development initiatives. This position is responsible for program planning, implementation, evaluation, and compliance across all major 4-H program areas. The Assistant Head works collaboratively with Extension faculty, staff, and volunteers to ensure high-quality, research-based youth programming that aligns with organizational goals and federal and state requirements. This is a 12-month position that reports directly to the Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development. Photographer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The photographer works to expand the state, regional and national visibility of Mississippi State University through conceiving, executing and delivering high-quality, professional images that align with the university mission and the current branding campaign. The photographer covers all areas of the university, including a variety of indoor and outdoor events, some of which require availability outside regular work hours and minimal travel. Photographic collaboration with the support of all campus partners is expected. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 63b95c20 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Intermittent Worker Intermittent Worker Employment Type Intermittent Intermittent Locations Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States Riley Center - Meridian, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) a25e927d Last Name (required) 62269d33 Email (required) 814a8e15 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\