    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/anesthesia-technician-trainee-i-or-ii-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Anesthesia Technician (Trainee, I, or II) - Main Campus",
      "description": "Anesthesia Technician (Trainee, I, or II) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Anesthesia Technician (Trainee, I, or II) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Anesthesia Technician (Trainee, I, or II) 507860 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 184000 - CVM Clinical Science Department Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Jun 13 2024 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: To administer anesthetics to render patients insensitive to pain during surgical and other medical procedures, supervise/teach students in the practice of anesthesia, maintain equipment and keep related records. Salary Grade : 12 Please see Staff Compensation Structure for salary ranges. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Set up and prepare anesthesia equipment prior to surgeries or other procedures. Set up appropriate monitoring equipment. Responsible for ensuring that anesthesia pharmacy supplies are adequately stocked and that all drugs are secure and accounted for. Instruct veterinary and veterinary technician students on correct procedures for administering anesthesia, case management, assign grades to students based on performance. Supervise and assist students during the anesthetic period, during anesthesia inducement and during patient recovery from anesthesia. Perform anesthesia procedures, including examining, preparing and positioning patients, interpreting blood work and chemistries, selecting drug regime and administering anesthetics. Assist with the administering of Educational Commission for Foreign Veterinary Graduates (ECFVG) examination; evaluate participants based on performance. Maintain records of drugs used and report appropriate charges. Prepare anesthesia log book and review. Minimum Qualifications: Trainee Level: Must possess a veterinary technology or technician degree, Must obtain certification within 1 calendar year of hire. Level I : High School Diploma or Equivalent. Certification as a Veterinary Technician or Registered Nurse, 4 years of related experience. Level II: High School Diploma or Equivalent. Certification as a Veterinary Technician or Registered Nurse, 4 years of related experience, plus 3 years' experience as Anesthesia Technician I or 5 or more years' experience in private practice. Rank and salary will be commensurate with education and experience. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to work with all kinds of animals. Working knowledge of techniques of restraint, sedation, anesthesia and patient monitoring. Instructions for Applying: Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu . Please include cover letter and resume along with names and addresses of at least three references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 46bd0146 Last Name (required) 3f71812b Email (required) 762bd01b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Intermittent Worker Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi These positions will assist the Purchasing area of the College of Veterinary Medicine Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Assistant Head of 4-H at the MSUES Center for 4-H Youth Development provides leadership and administrative support for statewide 4-H youth development initiatives. This position is responsible for program planning, implementation, evaluation, and compliance across all major 4-H program areas. The Assistant Head works collaboratively with Extension faculty, staff, and volunteers to ensure high-quality, research-based youth programming that aligns with organizational goals and federal and state requirements. This is a 12-month position that reports directly to the Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development. Photographer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The photographer works to expand the state, regional and national visibility of Mississippi State University through conceiving, executing and delivering high-quality, professional images that align with the university mission and the current branding campaign. The photographer covers all areas of the university, including a variety of indoor and outdoor events, some of which require availability outside regular work hours and minimal travel. Photographic collaboration with the support of all campus partners is expected. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert d31423c2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Support Staff Support Staff Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 7b8aa109 Last Name (required) fd428b8d Email (required) 8c24df9a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
