    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/client-experience-coordinator-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Client Experience Coordinator - Main Campus",
      "description": "Client Experience Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Client Experience Coordinator - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Client Experience Coordinator 511019 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 185370 - CVM Development Professional Part-Time 12-Month Opening on: Jul 30 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Client Experience Coordinator is responsible for enhancing the overall experience of clients interacting with the College of Veterinary Medicine, ensuring consistent, compassionate, and service-oriented engagement across the clinical environment. This role supports a culture of excellence in service delivery and helps strengthen relationships with clients, stakeholders, and the broader community. This position includes promotion and support of the Coat of Excellence program, advancing recognition and reinforcement of exemplary service. This is a 50% appointment (approximately 20 hours per week) with an expected standard schedule of 11:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Salary Grade : 14 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Area of Specialization: Office of Development Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Foster a welcoming, professional, and client-centered experience throughout the Animal Health Center (AHC). • Collect, organize, analyze, and summarize client feedback to identify trends and opportunities for service improvement. • Forward advancement-related or donor-relevant feedback to the Development Office as appropriate • Communicate client concerns through established channels to support timely and consistent resolution. • Promote client feedback surveys to encourage participation and gather meaningful feedback. • Collect, organize, analyze, and report client survey results and feedback trends to support continuous improvement. • Escalate client centered issues through designated channels (hospital administrator or Kristie) to ensure consistency of service • Promote awareness of Coat of Excellence recognition program • Assist with additional client experience and service excellence initiatives as assigned May be responsible for training, assisting, or assigning tasks to others. May provide input to performance reviews of other employees. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in communication, business, public administration, veterinary technology or related discipline Preferred Qualifications: Healthcare or veterinary hospital client services (client relations, front desk leadership, patient/client experience coordination) or, Hospitality or guest services management (event service leadership with high-touch customer interaction) or, Donor relations or advancement support experience Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Experience in customer service, client relations, hospitality, healthcare administration, or higher education environments • Strong interpersonal and communication skills • Ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic, service-oriented environment • Strong organizational skills and attention to detail • Experience with donor recognition programs • Commitment to delivering a high standard of client-centered service • Flexibility to respond to time-sensitive needs and occasional events outside the standard schedule • Professional presence and strong emotional intelligence in high-touch environments • Ability to support a culture of accountability, respect, and service excellence Working Conditions and Physical Effort Frequent- External and internal imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; involves conflict-resolution or similar interactions involving emotional issues or stress on a regular basis; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor Job frequently requires talking, sitting, hearing, and handling objects with hands. Job occasionally requires standing, walking, reaching, and lifting up to 25 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu. Please include a cover letter and resume along with names and addresses of at least three references. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 80dd7798 Last Name (required) 4cb2e47a Email (required) 6aab2294 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Intermittent Worker Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi These positions will assist the Purchasing area of the College of Veterinary Medicine Assistant Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Assistant Head of 4-H at the MSUES Center for 4-H Youth Development provides leadership and administrative support for statewide 4-H youth development initiatives. This position is responsible for program planning, implementation, evaluation, and compliance across all major 4-H program areas. The Assistant Head works collaboratively with Extension faculty, staff, and volunteers to ensure high-quality, research-based youth programming that aligns with organizational goals and federal and state requirements. This is a 12-month position that reports directly to the Head, Center for 4-H Youth Development. Photographer Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The photographer works to expand the state, regional and national visibility of Mississippi State University through conceiving, executing and delivering high-quality, professional images that align with the university mission and the current branding campaign. The photographer covers all areas of the university, including a variety of indoor and outdoor events, some of which require availability outside regular work hours and minimal travel. Photographic collaboration with the support of all campus partners is expected. Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 04be4ab5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Part-Time 12-Month Part-Time 12-Month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 0c994d50 Last Name (required) 3646e193 Email (required) e3f7c19c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
